{"openapi":"3.1.0","info":{"title":"Verified Handles API","version":"1.5.0","description":"Verified Handles as data: every public entry, its handles and images, its history, and search. It answers with the same data as the pages, built by the same code. Entry text is CC0, except a description taken from Wikipedia, which is CC BY-SA 4.0 (`description_license`): where you show it, show the article (`description_source.url`), the licence by name with a link ([CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)), and “adapted from” when `description_source.adapted` is true, and share alike. Images are licensed by their owners, and each says how (`image_rights`). Email addresses are never published as data.\n\n**Keys.** An entry answers to its VHID (11 digits, permanent), its short name, or an old name.\n\n**Paging.** Lists page by `limit` and `offset`; follow `next_offset` until it is null. Offsets stop at 10,000: past that they are clamped, silently.\n\n**Caching.** Responses say how long they may be kept (`Cache-Control`, and `x-cache` on each operation). An entry carries a strong ETag: send it back as `If-None-Match` and an unchanged entry answers 304.\n\n**Cross-origin.** `/api/v1` answers any origin (`Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`, GET only, no credentials). The `.json` addresses beside the pages are same-origin.\n\n**Rate limit.** 120 requests a minute per IP address across the JSON reads; past it, a 429 with `Retry-After`.\n\n**Errors** are JSON: `{\"error\": \"<code>\"}`, with a field or two more where they help.","license":{"name":"CC0 1.0 (entry text, except a description taken from Wikipedia, which is CC BY-SA 4.0; images are licensed separately)","identifier":"CC0-1.0"}},"servers":[{"url":"https://verifiedhandles.org"}],"tags":[{"name":"Claiming an entry","description":"Proving that you run the person or organisation an entry is about."},{"name":"Drafts","description":"An edit to an entry you have started and not saved, kept with your account for 30 days after its last change."},{"name":"Proposing changes","description":"Asking for a change to an entry, or for a new entry, with an account: a reviewer looks at it before it goes live. Anyone with an account may propose."},{"name":"Your account","description":"Your own preferences."},{"name":"Entries","description":"An entry: who or what it is, its handles and its images."},{"name":"History","description":"Every revision of an entry: the history kept from the old wiki and each edit made since."},{"name":"Search","description":"Finding entries by name, words, a Wikidata QID or a VHID."},{"name":"About the API","description":"This document."},{"name":"Applying for an entry","description":"Applying for a new entry, with what shows it should have one."},{"name":"Entry manager","description":"One entry’s settings, its Wikidata item, merges, restores and bulk changes."},{"name":"Connecting an app","description":"The OAuth endpoints an MCP client uses to connect to a person’s account: where to send them to sign in (the discovery documents), its tokens, refreshing them, and disconnecting."},{"name":"Reporting an entry","description":"Telling the site that something on an entry is wrong, out of date or abusive."}],"paths":{"/api/entity/{vhid}/claims":{"post":{"operationId":"startClaim","tags":["Claiming an entry"],"summary":"Start a claim","description":"Starts proving that you run the person or organisation an entry is about. It answers a token: publish it on a page the entry lists (`url`), in a DNS TXT record of its website’s domain (`dns`); or, for `email`, no token is needed: your account’s verified email must be an address the entry lists, or admin@, administrator@, webmaster@, hostmaster@ or postmaster@ at a domain it lists. The site then checks it for itself. An entry closed to claims is refused. An entry someone else holds can be claimed too: its proof asks an administrator for a transfer.","parameters":[{"name":"vhid","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The entry’s VHID (11 digits).","schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\d{11}$"},"example":"53500361835"}],"requestBody":{"description":"How you will prove it. At most 16 KiB.","required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"method":{"type":"string","enum":["url","dns","email"]},"target":{"description":"For `url`, the page; for `dns`, the domain. Not used for `email`.","type":"string"}},"required":["method"],"additionalProperties":false},"example":{"method":"url","target":"https://x.com/james"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The claim, with its token.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ClaimStarted"},"examples":{"url":{"summary":"By a page the entry lists","description":"POST /api/entity/53500361835/claims","value":{"ok":true,"claimId":"43","token":"vh-verify-7aa3f3873f6f706e0002d9de8eabb5cc","expires_at":"2026-10-12T09:00:00.000Z","method":"url","instructions":"Post this verification token on the profile/page listed on this entry, then verify: vh-verify-7aa3f3873f6f706e0002d9de8eabb5cc"}}}}}},"400":{"description":"The body is not JSON, the method is not one of the three, or `url`/`dns` came without a target. Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["bad_json","bad_method","target_required"],"description":"What is wrong with the body."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]},"examples":{"no-target":{"summary":"A page method with no page","description":"POST /api/entity/53500361835/claims","value":{"error":"target_required"}}}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"The entry takes no claims (`closed`). A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["closed"],"description":"The entry takes no claims."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"404":{"description":"No public entry has that VHID.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/NotFound"}}}},"413":{"description":"The body is over 16 KiB.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["too_large"],"description":"The body is too large."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many changes in the last minute: counted per IP address, per account and per key (an admin key’s per key alone, at the limit set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":"claim","x-read-only-key":false,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"mutation"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/api/claims/{id}/verify":{"post":{"operationId":"verifyClaim","tags":["Claiming an entry"],"summary":"Check a claim’s proof","description":"Checks the claim’s proof by its method: the token on the page the entry lists (`url`, fetched once, through the same guard as every fetch the site makes), in a DNS TXT record (`dns`), or your account’s verified email being an address the entry lists or a role address (admin@, administrator@, webmaster@, hostmaster@, postmaster@) at a domain it lists (`email`). Found, the entry is claimed at once: it is yours, and the Wikidata sync stops changing it (unless it is locked to admins). Found on an entry someone else holds: 202 `{\"review\":\"transfer\"}`, and an administrator decides the transfer in the review queue; nothing changes until then. Any other address at a domain the entry lists is not proof, but evidence: 202 `{\"review\":\"domain\"}`, for an administrator to decide. Either way the claimant is emailed the decision, and checking again answers the same 202. Not found: 422, with what was seen, and the claim stays open to check again until it expires. Its submitter may check it, and so may a reviewer.","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The claim’s id (`claimId` when it was started).","schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\d+$"},"example":"43"}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The proof was found: the entry is claimed.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"ok":{"type":"boolean","const":true},"vhid":{"type":"string"}},"required":["ok","vhid"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"202":{"description":"Filed for an administrator: a passing proof on an entry someone else holds (`transfer`), or an ordinary address at a listed domain (`domain`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"review":{"type":"string","enum":["transfer","domain"]}},"required":["review"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"400":{"description":"The claim’s entry is gone (`no_entity`) or its proof is unusable (`bad_evidence`). Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["no_entity","bad_evidence"],"description":"The claim’s entry is gone, or its stored proof is unusable."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"Not your claim and not a reviewer (`forbidden`), or the entry takes no claims now (`closed`). A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["closed"],"description":"The entry takes no claims now."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"404":{"description":"No such claim.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/NotFound"},"examples":{"missing":{"summary":"No such claim","description":"POST /api/claims/999999999/verify","value":{"error":"not_found"}}}}}},"409":{"description":"Already decided (`already_decided`), or decided or deleted while the proof ran (`conflict`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["already_decided","conflict"],"description":"Why not."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"410":{"description":"The token expired: start the claim again.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["expired"],"description":"Expired."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"422":{"description":"The token was not found: `detail` says what was seen. Put it in place and check again.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"ok":{"type":"boolean","const":false},"detail":{"type":"string"}},"required":["ok","detail"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many changes in the last minute: counted per IP address, per account and per key (an admin key’s per key alone, at the limit set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":"claim","x-read-only-key":false,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":null,"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/api/entity/{vhid}/draft":{"put":{"operationId":"putEntryDraft","tags":["Drafts"],"summary":"Keep a draft of an entry","description":"Keeps your unsaved edit to the entry, replacing any draft of it you had, and moves its expiry to 30 days from now. The description is cleaned with the same allowlist as a saved one. The body may be at most 256 KiB, and you may keep up to 100 drafts at once. A deleted entry takes no draft. Drafts are not in the audit log.","parameters":[{"name":"vhid","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The entry’s VHID (11 digits).","schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\d{11}$"}}],"requestBody":{"description":"The draft, and what it was edited against.","required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"draft":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EntryDraft"},"base_revision_id":{"description":"The revision the edit started from (the editor’s base revision), or null.","anyOf":[{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\d+$"},{"type":"null"}]}},"required":["draft"],"additionalProperties":false},"example":{"draft":{"fields":{"title":"James Haworth","subtitle":"Founder of Verified Handles"}},"base_revision_id":null}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Kept.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"ok":{"type":"boolean","const":true},"vhid":{"type":"string"},"base_revision_id":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\d+$"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The revision the draft was edited against, or null."},"saved_at":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"Its last change."},"expires_at":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"When it is deleted unless changed again: 30 days after `saved_at`."}},"required":["ok","vhid","base_revision_id","saved_at","expires_at"],"additionalProperties":false},"examples":{"keep":{"summary":"A changed subtitle","description":"PUT /api/entity/53500361835/draft","value":{"ok":true,"vhid":"53500361835","base_revision_id":null,"saved_at":"2026-10-06T12:00:00.000Z","expires_at":"2026-11-05T12:00:00.000Z"}}}}}},"400":{"description":"`bad_json`: the body is not JSON. `bad_payload`: the body or the draft is not the editor’s shape; `field` names the part. `bad_base_revision`: `base_revision_id` is not one of this entry’s revisions. Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["bad_json","bad_base_revision"],"description":"What was wrong."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","const":"bad_payload"},"field":{"type":"string","description":"The part that was wrong, e.g. `handles` or `fields.title`."}},"required":["error","field"],"additionalProperties":false}]},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]},"examples":{"bad":{"summary":"A key the editor does not write","description":"PUT /api/entity/53500361835/draft","value":{"error":"bad_payload","field":"colour"}}}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"404":{"description":"No entry has that VHID (`not_found`), or it is deleted.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["not_found"],"description":"No such entry."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"409":{"description":"You already keep 100 drafts: save or discard one first.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["too_many_drafts"],"description":"Too many drafts."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"413":{"description":"The body is over 256 KiB.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["too_large"],"description":"The body is too large."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many changes in the last minute: counted per IP address, per account and per key (an admin key’s per key alone, at the limit set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":false,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"mutation"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false},"get":{"operationId":"getEntryDraft","tags":["Drafts"],"summary":"Read your draft of an entry","description":"Your unsaved edit to the entry, as you last kept it, in the editor’s own shape.","parameters":[{"name":"vhid","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The entry’s VHID (11 digits).","schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\d{11}$"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The draft.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"vhid":{"type":"string"},"base_revision_id":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\d+$"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The revision the draft was edited against, or null."},"saved_at":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"Its last change."},"expires_at":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"When it is deleted unless changed again: 30 days after `saved_at`."},"draft":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EntryDraft"}},"required":["vhid","base_revision_id","saved_at","expires_at","draft"],"additionalProperties":false},"examples":{"mine":{"summary":"The draft kept above","description":"GET /api/entity/53500361835/draft","value":{"vhid":"53500361835","base_revision_id":null,"saved_at":"2026-10-06T12:00:00.000Z","expires_at":"2026-11-05T12:00:00.000Z","draft":{"fields":{"title":"James Haworth","subtitle":"Founder of Verified Handles"},"vhid":"53500361835","savedAt":1791288000000}}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"404":{"description":"No entry has that VHID (`not_found`), or you keep no draft of it, or it expired (`no_draft`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["not_found","no_draft"],"description":"What was not found."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":null,"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false},"delete":{"operationId":"deleteEntryDraft","tags":["Drafts"],"summary":"Discard your draft of an entry","description":"Deletes your draft of the entry, a deleted entry’s too. `deleted` is false when there was none to delete.","parameters":[{"name":"vhid","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The entry’s VHID (11 digits).","schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\d{11}$"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Done.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"ok":{"type":"boolean","const":true},"deleted":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["ok","deleted"],"additionalProperties":false},"examples":{"discard":{"summary":"The draft kept above","description":"DELETE /api/entity/53500361835/draft","value":{"ok":true,"deleted":true}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"404":{"description":"No entry has that VHID (`not_found`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["not_found"],"description":"No such entry."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many changes in the last minute: counted per IP address, per account and per key (an admin key’s per key alone, at the limit set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":false,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"mutation"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/api/entity/drafts":{"get":{"operationId":"listEntryDrafts","tags":["Drafts"],"summary":"List your drafts","description":"Every draft you keep, the most recently changed first, without their contents.","parameters":[],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Your drafts.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"drafts":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DraftListItem"}}},"required":["drafts"],"additionalProperties":false},"examples":{"mine":{"summary":"The one draft kept above","description":"GET /api/entity/drafts","value":{"drafts":[{"vhid":"53500361835","short":"james","title":"James Haworth","base_revision_id":null,"saved_at":"2026-10-06T12:00:00.000Z","expires_at":"2026-11-05T12:00:00.000Z","available":true}]}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":null,"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/api/editor/{vhid}":{"get":{"operationId":"getEditorContext","tags":["Proposing changes"],"summary":"Read an entry for editing","description":"What the editor opens with: the fields a change may send, as they are now, the current revision to send as `base_revision_id`, each handle with who manages it, the platforms, and what the caller may do (`capabilities`). Signed in, it carries your own unsaved draft of the entry too (`draft`). Signed out it answers too, with every capability false. Read it before proposing a change. An email address is shown only to a caller who may edit the entry live; anyone else gets it masked, and sends it back as it came to keep it.","parameters":[{"name":"vhid","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The entry’s VHID (11 digits). These routes take no short name.","schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\d{11}$"},"example":"53500361835"}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The entry, for editing.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EditorContext"}}}},"400":{"description":"Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"404":{"description":"No public entry has that VHID.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/NotFound"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{},{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"optional","x-rate-limit":null,"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/api/entity/{vhid}/revisions/{ref}":{"get":{"operationId":"getRevisionState","tags":["Proposing changes"],"summary":"Read an entry as it was","description":"The whole entry as it was at one revision made on Verified Handles, for proposing to put it back. History kept from the old wiki is wikitext, not fields: `not_restorable`. A hidden revision is `not_found`. An email address is masked, as in the editor’s context, for an account that may not edit the entry live.","parameters":[{"name":"vhid","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The entry’s VHID (11 digits). These routes take no short name.","schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\d{11}$"},"example":"53500361835"},{"name":"ref","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The revision, `r<n>`, as the entry’s history names it.","schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^r\\d+$"},"example":"r1"}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The entry as it was.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/RevisionState"},"examples":{"james":{"summary":"The first revision","description":"GET /api/entity/53500361835/revisions/r1","value":{"vhid":"53500361835","revision":{"ref_id":"r1","ts":"2026-09-19T12:00:00.000Z","summary":null,"hidden":false},"fields":{"title":"James Haworth","subtitle":null,"description":null,"short":"james","image_id":"3","gallery":[],"image_links":{},"custom_handle_order":false},"handles":[{"platform_id":"twitter","value":"james","display":null},{"platform_id":"instagram","value":"jameshaworth","display":null},{"platform_id":"linkedin","value":"james-haworth","display":null},{"platform_id":"email","value":null,"display":null,"masked":true,"ref":"4"}],"unavailable_images":[]}}}}}},"400":{"description":"The revision is not one made on Verified Handles (`not_restorable`). Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["not_restorable"],"description":"The revision is not one made on Verified Handles."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]},"examples":{"archive":{"summary":"Not a revision made here","description":"GET /api/entity/53500361835/revisions/a1","value":{"error":"not_restorable"}}}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"The account may not propose to this entry. A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["forbidden"],"description":"The account may not propose to this entry."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"404":{"description":"No public entry has that VHID, or no visible revision has that id.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/NotFound"}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many changes in the last minute: counted per IP address, per account and per key (an admin key’s per key alone, at the limit set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":"propose","x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"mutation"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/api/entity/search":{"get":{"operationId":"searchEntriesToLink","tags":["Proposing changes"],"summary":"Find an entry to link to","description":"The editor’s link search: up to 8 entries by name, words or QID, for a link in a description. Unlike the public search it is never cached, so an entry made a moment ago is found. A word the site does not search for answers an empty list.","parameters":[{"name":"q","in":"query","required":true,"description":"What to look for. Trimmed and cut to 200 characters; empty answers an empty list.","schema":{"type":"string","maxLength":200},"example":"james"}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The best matches first.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/LinkSearch"},"examples":{"james":{"summary":"By name","description":"GET /api/entity/search?q=james","value":{"results":[{"vhid":"53500361835","title":"James Haworth","subtitle":null,"short":"james"}]}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]},"examples":{"signed-out":{"summary":"With no key","description":"GET /api/entity/search?q=james","value":{"error":"auth_required"}}}}}},"403":{"description":"A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many changes in the last minute: counted per IP address, per account and per key (an admin key’s per key alone, at the limit set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"mutation"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/api/entity/{vhid}/proposals":{"post":{"operationId":"proposeChange","tags":["Proposing changes"],"summary":"Propose a change to an entry","description":"Queues a change for a reviewer, who approves it into the entry or turns it down. Send only the fields that change, with the `baseRevisionId` you read as `base_revision_id`. Proposing the same change again while it waits answers the same proposal. `qid_link` proposes linking the entry to a Wikidata item (or, with `qid: null`, unlinking it). Handle ops (`add_handles` / `remove_handles`) are stored as ops and applied to the entry’s list as it is when the proposal is approved, so two proposals adding different handles both apply; a proposal of nothing but ops is never held to its base revision, and one whose every op would change nothing now is refused (`no_changes`). Takes an optional `Idempotency-Key`, so a request whose answer was lost can be sent again safely: the retry gets the first answer back.","parameters":[{"name":"vhid","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The entry’s VHID (11 digits). These routes take no short name.","schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\d{11}$"},"example":"53500361835"},{"name":"Idempotency-Key","in":"header","required":false,"description":"A key you choose for this one request (1–255 printable ASCII characters, e.g. a UUID). Send the same request with the same key again, within 24 hours, and the first answer comes back (`Idempotency-Replayed: true`) with nothing written again. The key is your account’s and this route’s alone. \"The same request\" is the same path and the same JSON (key order and spacing aside; `base_revision_id` aside, so a retry made after re-reading the entry still matches). Only a 2xx answer is kept: after any other, nothing was written and the key is free to retry.","schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[\\x20-\\x7E]{1,255}$"},"example":"0f8b3c5e-1d2a-4e7b-9c61-5a4d3e2f1b0a"}],"requestBody":{"description":"The change, under `payload` (or the change itself as the body).","required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"payload":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EditPayload"},"base_revision_id":{"description":"The revision the change was made against (`baseRevisionId`).","type":"string"},"prepared_by":{"description":"Sent by the site’s own pages when an AI agent in the person’s browser prepared the change (WebMCP). Recorded on the audit row, and on a proposal shown to its reviewer; it changes nothing else. Any other value is ignored.","type":"string","const":"webmcp"},"qid_link":{"type":"object","properties":{"qid":{"description":"The item, `Q<n>`; null or empty unlinks.","type":["string","null"]},"adopt":{"description":"Fields to take from the item when the link is approved.","type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["qid"],"additionalProperties":false}},"required":["payload"],"additionalProperties":false},"example":{"payload":{"subtitle":"Founder of Verified Handles"},"base_revision_id":"1"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Queued.","headers":{"Idempotency-Replayed":{"description":"`true` when this is the stored answer to an earlier request with the same Idempotency-Key: nothing was written now.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ProposalQueued"},"examples":{"subtitle":{"summary":"Propose a subtitle","description":"POST /api/entity/53500361835/proposals","value":{"ok":true,"submissionId":"41","status":"pending"}}}}}},"400":{"description":"The change is malformed, would change nothing, or names a platform the catalog does not have or has disabled (`invalid_platform`). Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one. Or the Idempotency-Key is not 1–255 printable ASCII characters (`bad_idempotency_key`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","description":"`bad_json`: the body is not JSON. `bad_payload`: a field has the wrong type. `<field>_too_long`: a field is over 64 KiB. `blocked_content`: the text has a word the site does not take. Others name what is wrong: `invalid_image`, `invalid_image_link`, `no_changes`, a website that can never link. `invalid_platform`: a handle names a platform the catalog does not have, or a new handle is on a disabled one (a handle the entry already has on it is kept); `field`, `platform_id`, `reason` and `message` say which. `handles_with_ops`: `handles` beside `add_handles` / `remove_handles`. `masked_handle_needs_ref`: an email the caller may not see named by an address. A `no_changes` of handle ops says what each came to (`handle_ops`)."},"field":{"description":"With `invalid_platform`: the handle, as `handles[<i>].platform_id` (or `add_handles[<i>]…`).","type":"string"},"platform_id":{"description":"With `invalid_platform`: the platform id refused.","type":"string"},"reason":{"description":"With `invalid_platform`: the catalog has no such platform (`unknown`), or it is disabled (`disabled`).","type":"string","enum":["unknown","disabled"]},"message":{"description":"With `invalid_platform`: the refusal in words, naming the id and where the platform ids are listed (MCP `platform_catalog`).","type":"string"},"handle_ops":{"description":"With `no_changes` from handle ops: each one a no-op.","$ref":"#/components/schemas/HandleOpsReport"}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["bad_idempotency_key","idempotency_key_reused","idempotency_key_in_progress"],"description":"What was wrong with the Idempotency-Key."},"message":{"type":"string","description":"The refusal in words."}},"required":["error","message"],"additionalProperties":false}]},"examples":{"bad":{"summary":"A field of the wrong type","description":"POST /api/entity/53500361835/proposals","value":{"error":"bad_payload"}},"ops-and-list":{"summary":"The whole handle list beside handle ops","description":"POST /api/entity/53500361835/proposals","value":{"error":"handles_with_ops"}},"platform":{"summary":"A handle on a platform the catalog does not have","description":"POST /api/entity/53500361835/proposals","value":{"error":"invalid_platform","field":"handles[0].platform_id","platform_id":"twiter","reason":"unknown","message":"handles[0].platform_id: \"twiter\" is not a platform in the catalog. Use a platform id from the platform catalog (MCP: platform_catalog, or get_entry with include_platforms)."}}}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"The entry takes no proposals from this account (`forbidden`), or a link on an image needs `link_images`. A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["image_link_forbidden"],"description":"A link on an image needs the `link_images` capability."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"404":{"description":"No public entry has that VHID.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/NotFound"}}}},"409":{"description":"The Wikipedia page named in `wikipedia_credit` cannot be credited: missing, not an article or a draft, a section, no lead, a draft of an item that has an article, or the description is not the page’s text (`credit_text_differs`). Or the first request with this Idempotency-Key is still running (`idempotency_key_in_progress`): try again after `Retry-After` seconds.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"With `idempotency_key_in_progress`: seconds to wait.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","description":"Why the named page cannot be credited (see `wikipedia_credit`)."},"page":{"description":"The page Wikipedia resolved the name to.","type":"string"},"share":{"description":"With `credit_text_differs`: the share (0–1) of the description’s phrases that are the page’s.","type":"number"},"article":{"description":"With `draft_has_article`: the item’s English article.","type":"string"}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["bad_idempotency_key","idempotency_key_reused","idempotency_key_in_progress"],"description":"What was wrong with the Idempotency-Key."},"message":{"type":"string","description":"The refusal in words."}},"required":["error","message"],"additionalProperties":false}]}}}},"413":{"description":"The body is over 512 KiB.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["too_large"],"description":"The body is too large."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"422":{"description":"This Idempotency-Key was used for a different request in the last 24 hours (`idempotency_key_reused`): nothing was written.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["bad_idempotency_key","idempotency_key_reused","idempotency_key_in_progress"],"description":"What was wrong with the Idempotency-Key."},"message":{"type":"string","description":"The refusal in words."}},"required":["error","message"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many changes in the last minute: counted per IP address, per account and per key (an admin key’s per key alone, at the limit set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"502":{"description":"Wikipedia (or Wikidata) did not answer the read of a named page: try again.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["wikipedia_unreachable"],"description":"Upstream."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":"propose","x-read-only-key":false,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"mutation"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/api/entity":{"post":{"operationId":"proposeNewEntry","tags":["Proposing changes"],"summary":"Propose a new entry","description":"Queues a new entry for a reviewer. Give it a title and, if it has one, its Wikidata item (`qid`); an entry already on that item is named instead (409), and an item Wikidata has merged into another is refused (409 `qid_merged`, `wikidata_item` names the one it kept: propose on that). A new entry has no images until it exists. While new entries are paused, it answers 503 `not_accepting`. (An account that may create entries itself is not paused.) A short a site redirect holds is refused (409 `short_is_redirect`). With `?check=1` it runs every check and queues nothing: 200 `{ ok: true, check: true }`, or the refusal the real call would answer (an `Idempotency-Key` is not recorded for it). Takes an optional `Idempotency-Key`, so a request whose answer was lost can be sent again safely: the retry gets the first answer back.","parameters":[{"name":"check","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Send `1` to check the proposal without queueing it, or leave it out; any other value is `bad_check` (400).","schema":{"type":"string","const":"1"}},{"name":"Idempotency-Key","in":"header","required":false,"description":"A key you choose for this one request (1–255 printable ASCII characters, e.g. a UUID). Send the same request with the same key again, within 24 hours, and the first answer comes back (`Idempotency-Replayed: true`) with nothing written again. The key is your account’s and this route’s alone. \"The same request\" is the same path and the same JSON (key order and spacing aside; `base_revision_id` aside, so a retry made after re-reading the entry still matches). Only a 2xx answer is kept: after any other, nothing was written and the key is free to retry.","schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[\\x20-\\x7E]{1,255}$"},"example":"0f8b3c5e-1d2a-4e7b-9c61-5a4d3e2f1b0a"}],"requestBody":{"description":"The new entry, under `payload`, and its Wikidata item.","required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"payload":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EditPayload"},"qid":{"description":"Its Wikidata item, `Q<n>`. One that is sent must be a real QID.","type":["string","null"]}},"required":["payload"],"additionalProperties":false},"example":{"payload":{"title":"Ada Lovelace","subtitle":"Mathematician"},"qid":"Q7259"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Queued; or with `?check=1`, it would be (nothing is queued).","headers":{"Idempotency-Replayed":{"description":"`true` when this is the stored answer to an earlier request with the same Idempotency-Key: nothing was written now.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ProposalQueued"},{"type":"object","properties":{"ok":{"type":"boolean","const":true},"check":{"type":"boolean","const":true}},"required":["ok","check"],"additionalProperties":false}]},"examples":{"ada":{"summary":"Propose an entry for a Wikidata item","description":"POST /api/entity","value":{"ok":true,"submissionId":"42","status":"pending"}},"check":{"summary":"Check a proposal without queueing it","description":"POST /api/entity?check=1","value":{"ok":true,"check":true}}}}}},"400":{"description":"The proposal is malformed: no title (`title_required`), a bad QID (`bad_qid`), an image (`image_on_new_entry`), a Wikipedia credit (`credit_on_new_entry`: name it once the entry exists), a handle on a platform the catalog does not have or has disabled (`invalid_platform`, naming it), a field of the wrong type, or a `check` that is not `1` (`bad_check`). Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one. Or the Idempotency-Key is not 1–255 printable ASCII characters (`bad_idempotency_key`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","description":"`bad_json`: the body is not JSON. `bad_payload`: a field has the wrong type. `<field>_too_long`: a field is over 64 KiB. `blocked_content`: the text has a word the site does not take. Others name what is wrong: `invalid_image`, `invalid_image_link`, `no_changes`, a website that can never link. `invalid_platform`: a handle names a platform the catalog does not have, or a new handle is on a disabled one (a handle the entry already has on it is kept); `field`, `platform_id`, `reason` and `message` say which. `handles_with_ops`: `handles` beside `add_handles` / `remove_handles`. `masked_handle_needs_ref`: an email the caller may not see named by an address. A `no_changes` of handle ops says what each came to (`handle_ops`)."},"field":{"description":"With `invalid_platform`: the handle, as `handles[<i>].platform_id` (or `add_handles[<i>]…`).","type":"string"},"platform_id":{"description":"With `invalid_platform`: the platform id refused.","type":"string"},"reason":{"description":"With `invalid_platform`: the catalog has no such platform (`unknown`), or it is disabled (`disabled`).","type":"string","enum":["unknown","disabled"]},"message":{"description":"With `invalid_platform`: the refusal in words, naming the id and where the platform ids are listed (MCP `platform_catalog`).","type":"string"},"handle_ops":{"description":"With `no_changes` from handle ops: each one a no-op.","$ref":"#/components/schemas/HandleOpsReport"}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["bad_idempotency_key","idempotency_key_reused","idempotency_key_in_progress"],"description":"What was wrong with the Idempotency-Key."},"message":{"type":"string","description":"The refusal in words."}},"required":["error","message"],"additionalProperties":false}]},"examples":{"untitled":{"summary":"No title","description":"POST /api/entity","value":{"error":"title_required"}}}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"The account may not propose (`forbidden`). A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"409":{"description":"An entry is already on that Wikidata item (perhaps a deleted one): it is named (`already_exists`). Or Wikidata has merged the item into another (`qid_merged`): `wikidata_item` names the item it kept, and nothing is queued. Or the short is the address of a site redirect (`short_is_redirect`): choose another, or an administrator deletes the redirect first. Or the first request with this Idempotency-Key is still running (`idempotency_key_in_progress`): try again after `Retry-After` seconds.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"With `idempotency_key_in_progress`: seconds to wait.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","const":"already_exists"},"entry":{"type":"object","properties":{"vhid":{"type":"string"},"short":{"type":["string","null"]},"title":{"type":"string"}},"required":["vhid","short","title"],"additionalProperties":false}},"required":["error","entry"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","const":"qid_merged"},"qid":{"type":"string"},"wikidata_item":{"type":"string"},"message":{"type":"string"},"retry":{"type":"boolean","const":false}},"required":["error","qid","wikidata_item","message","retry"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","const":"short_is_redirect"}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false}]},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["bad_idempotency_key","idempotency_key_reused","idempotency_key_in_progress"],"description":"What was wrong with the Idempotency-Key."},"message":{"type":"string","description":"The refusal in words."}},"required":["error","message"],"additionalProperties":false}]}}}},"413":{"description":"The body is over 512 KiB.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["too_large"],"description":"The body is too large."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"422":{"description":"This Idempotency-Key was used for a different request in the last 24 hours (`idempotency_key_reused`): nothing was written.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["bad_idempotency_key","idempotency_key_reused","idempotency_key_in_progress"],"description":"What was wrong with the Idempotency-Key."},"message":{"type":"string","description":"The refusal in words."}},"required":["error","message"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many changes in the last minute: counted per IP address, per account and per key (an admin key’s per key alone, at the limit set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"New entries are paused (`not_accepting`, JSON), or the site is down for maintenance (an HTML page). Try again later.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/NotAccepting"}}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":"propose","x-read-only-key":false,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"mutation"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/api/entity/batch":{"post":{"operationId":"editEntriesBatch","tags":["Proposing changes"],"summary":"Propose or make many changes at once","description":"Up to 25 edits in one request, each to a different entry: all proposals (`mode: \"propose\"`, as `POST /api/entity/{vhid}/proposals`) or all live edits (`mode: \"live\"`, as the editor’s Save makes them). Each edit is judged and made exactly as the single route makes it: whether this account may (entry by entry: a live edit needs `edit_live`, or `edit_locked` on an entry locked to admins), the conflict check against `base_revision_id`, one revision and one audit row per entry. A batch grants nothing a single call would refuse. One thing it refuses that a single call takes: naming a Wikipedia page for the credit (`credit_in_batch`), which the server reads from Wikipedia; send that one alone.\n\n**One at a time** (the default): each edit in its own transaction, in order. One edit refused leaves the others made; the answer is 200 with each edit’s outcome, in request order, with the code and status the single route would have answered.\n\n**`atomic: true`**: all or nothing. Every entry is locked first, in VHID order, and any refused edit undoes the whole batch: 422 `batch_failed`, naming every refused edit and why; the rest are `not_applied`, and nothing is written.\n\n**Replaying** a batch whose answer was lost is safe: an edit already made answers `conflict`, with `revisions_since_base: 1` and `all_since_base_by_you: true`; a proposal already filed answers its own `submission_id`. Every audit row of a batch carries its `batch_id`.\n\n**Rate limit.** Every edit counts as one change against the IP address, account and key, so 25 edits cost what they would cost sent one by one; the request is refused (429) before any edit runs when they do not fit. Takes an optional `Idempotency-Key`, so a request whose answer was lost can be sent again safely: the retry gets the first answer back.","parameters":[{"name":"Idempotency-Key","in":"header","required":false,"description":"A key you choose for this one request (1–255 printable ASCII characters, e.g. a UUID). Send the same request with the same key again, within 24 hours, and the first answer comes back (`Idempotency-Replayed: true`) with nothing written again. The key is your account’s and this route’s alone. \"The same request\" is the same path and the same JSON (key order and spacing aside; `base_revision_id` aside, so a retry made after re-reading the entry still matches). Only a 2xx answer is kept: after any other, nothing was written and the key is free to retry.","schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[\\x20-\\x7E]{1,255}$"},"example":"0f8b3c5e-1d2a-4e7b-9c61-5a4d3e2f1b0a"}],"requestBody":{"description":"The batch.","required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"mode":{"type":"string","enum":["live","propose"],"description":"Live edits or proposals: one kind per batch."},"atomic":{"description":"All or nothing. Default false: each edit on its own.","type":"boolean"},"summary":{"description":"Each live edit’s why, unless it gives its own. A proposal takes none.","type":"string","maxLength":500},"edits":{"minItems":1,"maxItems":25,"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"title":{"type":"string"},"subtitle":{"type":["string","null"]},"description":{"description":"HTML, sanitised on the way in by the same allowlist as every description. At most 64 KiB.","type":["string","null"]},"description_source":{"description":"Only `null`, which takes the \"from Wikipedia\" credit off. A credit is never sent: name its page with `wikipedia_credit`.","type":"null"},"wikipedia_credit":{"description":"Credit the description “from Wikipedia”. The server reads the page itself (redirects followed, so a draft since moved is its article), and refuses it unless at least half of the description’s three-word phrases are the page’s lead (`409 credit_text_differs`, with `page` and `share`). Not with `description_source: null`. Errors: `400 bad_wikipedia_title` / `not_english_wikipedia`; `409 wikipedia_page_missing`, `wikipedia_namespace` (not an article or a draft), `wikipedia_section`, `wikipedia_no_lead`, `no_description`, `draft_has_article` (the entry’s item already has an English article, named in `article`: credit that); `502 wikipedia_unreachable`.","type":"object","properties":{"page":{"type":"string","description":"An English Wikipedia article or draft, by title (`Draft:Dominic McLaughlin`) or address (`https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/…`)."},"let_wikidata_manage":{"description":"For a draft only: `false` keeps the description site-authored. By default a draft’s credit hands the description to the Wikidata sync, which leaves it alone until the draft is an article linked from the entry’s Wikidata item.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["page"],"additionalProperties":false},"short":{"description":"The short name (`/<short>`); `null` removes it.","type":["string","null"]},"image_id":{"description":"The lead image, by media id; `null` removes it.","type":["string","null"]},"gallery":{"description":"The whole gallery after the lead, in order, by media id: it replaces the one there.","type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"image_links":{"description":"The whole map of links on the entry’s images, media id → absolute http(s) address. Needs the `link_images` capability.","type":"object","propertyNames":{"type":"string"},"additionalProperties":{"type":"string"}},"custom_handle_order":{"description":"Keep `handles` in the order given, rather than the site’s order.","type":"boolean"},"handles":{"description":"The whole list of handles, in order: it replaces the one there. Not with `add_handles` / `remove_handles`.","type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"platform_id":{"type":"string"},"value":{"type":"string"},"display":{"description":"A label to show instead of the value.","type":["string","null"]}},"required":["platform_id","value"],"additionalProperties":false}},"add_handles":{"description":"Handles to put on the entry, at the end of its list as it is when the change is applied (a proposal: when it is approved). One the entry has already (the same value, in any case the platform folds) changes nothing. No base revision is needed for it. Not with `handles` (400 `handles_with_ops`).","type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"platform_id":{"type":"string"},"value":{"type":"string","description":"Not blank. A website is completed to an address, as in `handles`."},"display":{"description":"A label to show instead of the value.","type":["string","null"]}},"required":["platform_id","value"],"additionalProperties":false}},"remove_handles":{"description":"Handles to take off, by value — or, for an email the caller may not see, by `ref` (an address is refused: `masked_handle_needs_ref`). One the entry does not have changes nothing. A value the Wikidata sync supplied is held back from it, as when a list leaves it out. Not with `handles`.","type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"platform_id":{"type":"string","description":"The platform’s id."},"value":{"description":"The handle, as stored or in any case the platform folds.","type":"string"},"ref":{"description":"Instead of `value`, for an email the caller may not see: the `ref` `GET /api/editor/{vhid}` gives it.","type":"string"}},"required":["platform_id"],"additionalProperties":false}},"relinquish":{"description":"Fields to hand back to the Wikidata sync.","type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"takeover":{"description":"Fields to take from the Wikidata sync, keeping their value.","type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"handle_takeover":{"description":"Handles to take from the Wikidata sync.","type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"platform_id":{"type":"string","description":"The platform’s id."},"value":{"type":"string","description":"The handle as stored."}},"required":["platform_id","value"],"additionalProperties":false}},"handle_relinquish":{"description":"Handles to hand to the Wikidata sync, while Wikidata lists them.","type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"platform_id":{"type":"string","description":"The platform’s id."},"value":{"type":"string","description":"The handle as stored."}},"required":["platform_id","value"],"additionalProperties":false}},"handle_release":{"description":"Values held back from the sync that it may add again.","type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"platform_id":{"type":"string","description":"The platform’s id."},"value":{"type":"string","description":"The handle as stored."}},"required":["platform_id","value"],"additionalProperties":false}},"vhid":{"type":"string","description":"The entry’s VHID (11 digits). Each entry at most once in a batch."},"base_revision_id":{"description":"The revision the change was made against (`baseRevisionId` of `GET /api/editor/{vhid}`): needed for a live edit, unless it is handle ops alone.","type":"string"},"summary":{"description":"A live edit’s why, shown in the history. Defaults to the batch’s `summary`.","type":"string","maxLength":500},"payload":{"description":"A proposal may nest its change under `payload`, as at `POST /api/entity/{vhid}/proposals`.","$ref":"#/components/schemas/EditPayload"},"qid_link":{"description":"A proposal’s Wikidata link, as at the single route.","type":"object","properties":{"qid":{"type":["string","null"]},"adopt":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["qid"],"additionalProperties":false}},"required":["vhid"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"One edit: its entry’s `vhid` beside exactly the body the single route takes — the editor’s live save for `live`, `POST /api/entity/{vhid}/proposals`’s for `propose`."}}},"required":["mode","edits"],"additionalProperties":false},"example":{"mode":"propose","edits":[{"vhid":"53500361835","payload":{"subtitle":"Founder of Verified Handles"},"base_revision_id":"1"},{"vhid":"00000000000","payload":{"subtitle":"No such entry"}}]}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Each edit’s outcome, in request order (one at a time, or an atomic batch that was made whole).","headers":{"Idempotency-Replayed":{"description":"`true` when this is the stored answer to an earlier request with the same Idempotency-Key: nothing was written now.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"batch_id":{"type":"string","description":"This batch, as its audit rows name it (`detail.batch`)."},"mode":{"type":"string","enum":["live","propose"]},"atomic":{"type":"boolean"},"succeeded":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"How many edits were made or filed."},"failed":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"How many were refused."},"results":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BatchEditResult"}}},"required":["batch_id","mode","atomic","succeeded","failed","results"],"additionalProperties":false},"examples":{"proposals":{"summary":"Two proposals at once, one to an entry that takes none from this account","description":"POST /api/entity/batch","value":{"batch_id":"1b9d6bcd-bbfd-4b2d-9b5d-ab8dfbbd4bed","mode":"propose","atomic":false,"succeeded":1,"failed":1,"results":[{"vhid":"53500361835","status":"ok","submission_id":"41"},{"vhid":"00000000000","status":"error","error":"not_found","http_status":404}]}},"liveRefused":{"summary":"Live edits from an account that may not edit the entry live: refused edit by edit","description":"POST /api/entity/batch","value":{"batch_id":"1b9d6bcd-bbfd-4b2d-9b5d-ab8dfbbd4bed","mode":"live","atomic":false,"succeeded":0,"failed":1,"results":[{"vhid":"53500361835","status":"error","error":"forbidden","http_status":403}]}}}}}},"400":{"description":"The request is not a batch: `bad_json`, `bad_mode` (not `live` or `propose`), `no_edits`, `too_many_edits` (more than 25), `bad_edit` (an edit with no `vhid`), `duplicate_vhid` (an entry twice), or `bad_payload` / `summary_too_long` for `atomic` or `summary`. Nothing ran. Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one. Or the Idempotency-Key is not 1–255 printable ASCII characters (`bad_idempotency_key`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["bad_json","bad_payload","bad_mode","no_edits","too_many_edits","bad_edit","duplicate_vhid","summary_too_long"],"description":"What is wrong with the batch itself."},"index":{"description":"With `bad_edit`: the edit with no `vhid`.","type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991},"vhid":{"description":"With `duplicate_vhid`: the entry named twice.","type":"string"},"max":{"description":"With `too_many_edits`: the most a batch takes.","type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991},"field":{"description":"With `bad_payload`: the field of the wrong type (`atomic`, `summary`).","type":"string"}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["bad_idempotency_key","idempotency_key_reused","idempotency_key_in_progress"],"description":"What was wrong with the Idempotency-Key."},"message":{"type":"string","description":"The refusal in words."}},"required":["error","message"],"additionalProperties":false}]},"examples":{"empty":{"summary":"No edits","description":"POST /api/entity/batch","value":{"error":"no_edits"}}}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"409":{"description":"The first request with this Idempotency-Key is still running (`idempotency_key_in_progress`): try again after `Retry-After` seconds.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"With `idempotency_key_in_progress`: seconds to wait.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["bad_idempotency_key","idempotency_key_reused","idempotency_key_in_progress"],"description":"What was wrong with the Idempotency-Key."},"message":{"type":"string","description":"The refusal in words."}},"required":["error","message"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"413":{"description":"The body is over 25 × 512 KiB. (One edit over 512 KiB is that edit’s `too_large`, 413.)","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["too_large"],"description":"The body is too large."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"422":{"description":"An atomic batch was refused whole: every refused edit named, the rest `not_applied`. Nothing was written. Or this Idempotency-Key was used for a different request in the last 24 hours (`idempotency_key_reused`): nothing was written.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","const":"batch_failed"},"mode":{"type":"string","enum":["live","propose"]},"atomic":{"type":"boolean","const":true},"failed":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"How many edits were refused."},"results":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BatchEditResult"}}},"required":["error","mode","atomic","failed","results"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["bad_idempotency_key","idempotency_key_reused","idempotency_key_in_progress"],"description":"What was wrong with the Idempotency-Key."},"message":{"type":"string","description":"The refusal in words."}},"required":["error","message"],"additionalProperties":false}]},"examples":{"atomic":{"summary":"All or nothing: one edit refused, so none is made","description":"POST /api/entity/batch","value":{"error":"batch_failed","mode":"propose","atomic":true,"failed":1,"results":[{"vhid":"53500361835","status":"not_applied"},{"vhid":"10000000001","status":"error","error":"bad_payload","http_status":400}]}}}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many changes in the last minute: counted per IP address, per account and per key (an admin key’s per key alone, at the limit set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":"propose","x-read-only-key":false,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"mutation"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/api/entity/description-preview":{"post":{"operationId":"previewDescription","tags":["Proposing changes"],"summary":"See a description as it would be stored","description":"The HTML a save would store for this description, and nothing written: the same steps a live edit or an approved proposal runs (`[[VHID]]` and `[[short]]` links made into links to the entry, `[url label]` into a link, then the site’s HTML allowlist, which drops a script, an event handler and any tag or attribute it does not keep). Console → Batch edit shows a new description with it before anything is sent. `html` is null when nothing would be left, which a save stores as no description. Counts as one change against the rate limit, as the writes it previews.","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"description":"The description, as an edit would send it: HTML, or the `[[…]]` and `[url label]` link forms.","required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"description":{"type":"string","description":"Up to 64 KiB in UTF-8, as a saved description."}},"required":["description"],"additionalProperties":false},"example":{"description":"<p>See <a href=\"https://example.org/\" onclick=\"steal()\">our site</a>.</p><script>alert(1)</script>"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The description as it would be stored.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"html":{"description":"The stored HTML; null when nothing would be left.","type":["string","null"]}},"required":["html"],"additionalProperties":false},"examples":{"sanitised":{"summary":"A link kept, its onclick and a script dropped","description":"POST /api/entity/description-preview","value":{"html":"<p>See <a href=\"https://example.org/\">our site</a>.</p>"}},"empty":{"summary":"Nothing left once the script is dropped","description":"POST /api/entity/description-preview","value":{"html":null}}}}}},"400":{"description":"The body is not JSON (`bad_json`), `description` is not a string (`bad_payload`), or it is over 64 KiB (`description_too_long`). Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["bad_json","bad_payload","description_too_long"],"description":"What is wrong with the request."},"field":{"description":"With `bad_payload`: `description`, which must be a string.","type":"string"}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]},"examples":{"signed-out":{"summary":"With no key","description":"POST /api/entity/description-preview","value":{"error":"auth_required"}}}}}},"403":{"description":"A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"413":{"description":"The body is over 512 KiB.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["too_large"],"description":"The body is too large."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many changes in the last minute: counted per IP address, per account and per key (an admin key’s per key alone, at the limit set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":"propose","x-read-only-key":false,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"mutation"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key is `no-store` with `Vary: Authorization`; to a signed-in session, `private, no-store`."},"x-cors":false}},"/api/media/library":{"get":{"operationId":"searchImageLibrary","tags":["Proposing changes"],"summary":"Find an image the site already holds","description":"The image picker’s “On Verified Handles” tab: images the site holds that may go on an entry (never a withdrawn one), found by the entries that show or showed them, a file name, a credit or licence, or `#<id>`. 24 to a page, newest first. Each says its licence and credit and which entries use it; a deleted entry is never named. Fewer than 2 characters finds nothing. Counted against the same per-account limit as changes, 60 a minute.","parameters":[{"name":"q","in":"query","required":true,"description":"What to look for, 2 to 200 characters.","schema":{"type":"string","maxLength":200},"example":"james"},{"name":"offset","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Results to skip; clamped to 10,000.","schema":{"default":0,"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":10000}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"A page of images.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"},"total":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991},"next_offset":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991},{"type":"null"}]},"results":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/LibraryImage"}}},"required":["query","total","next_offset","results"],"additionalProperties":false},"examples":{"short":{"summary":"Too short to look for","description":"GET /api/media/library?q=j","value":{"query":"j","total":0,"next_offset":null,"results":[]}}}}}},"400":{"description":"The text is over 200 characters (`query_too_long`). Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["query_too_long"],"description":"The text is over 200 characters."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":{}},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many changes in the last minute: counted per IP address, per account and per key (an admin key’s per key alone, at the limit set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"mutation"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/api/media/commons/search":{"get":{"operationId":"searchCommons","tags":["Proposing changes"],"summary":"Search Wikimedia Commons for an image","description":"The image picker’s Commons tab: up to 24 image files on Wikimedia Commons, each with a signed `token` that names it to the site. It asks Commons; when Commons does not answer in time, no results. A file name (with or without `File:`) also finds that exact file, first, even before Commons’ search has caught up with it. Files withdrawn or restricted here are left out. Fewer than 2 characters asks nothing. 60 a minute per account.","parameters":[{"name":"q","in":"query","required":true,"description":"What to look for, 2 to 200 characters.","schema":{"type":"string","maxLength":200},"example":"Ada Lovelace"}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The files.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"results":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/CommonsHit"}}},"required":["results"],"additionalProperties":false},"examples":{"short":{"summary":"Too short to ask Commons","description":"GET /api/media/commons/search?q=a","value":{"results":[]}}}}}},"400":{"description":"The text is over 200 characters (`query_too_long`). Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["query_too_long"],"description":"The text is over 200 characters."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":{}},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many changes in the last minute: counted per IP address, per account and per key (an admin key’s per key alone, at the limit set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"mutation"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/api/media/commons":{"post":{"operationId":"pickCommonsImage","tags":["Proposing changes"],"summary":"Choose a Commons file","description":"Turns a search hit’s `token` into an image the site holds, so a proposal can name it (`image_id`). The same file picked again answers the same image. It takes the token, never a file name: only a file a search found can be chosen.","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"description":"The hit’s token.","required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"token":{"type":"string"}},"required":["token"],"additionalProperties":false},"example":{"token":"not-a-token"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Held: its id.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"ok":{"type":"boolean","const":true},"mediaId":{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\d+$"},"filename":{"type":"string","description":"The file’s name, as Commons spells it."}},"required":["ok","mediaId","filename"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"400":{"description":"Not JSON (`bad_json`), no token (`bad_payload`), or the token is forged or expired (`bad_token`). Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["bad_json","bad_payload","bad_token"],"description":"`bad_json`, `bad_payload` (no token), `bad_token` (forged or expired)."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":{}},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]},"examples":{"bad-token":{"summary":"A token no search gave","description":"POST /api/media/commons","value":{"error":"bad_token"}}}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"409":{"description":"The file is withdrawn here (`image_withdrawn`), or restricted (`image_unavailable`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["image_withdrawn","image_unavailable"],"description":"Why not."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":{}}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many changes in the last minute: counted per IP address, per account and per key (an admin key’s per key alone, at the limit set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":false,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"mutation"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/api/user/prefs":{"get":{"operationId":"getPrefs","tags":["Your account"],"summary":"Read your preferences","description":"The preferences of the account the key belongs to. Signed out, it still answers 200, with every value null, so a client need not check first.","parameters":[],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The preferences.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Prefs"},"examples":{"signed-in":{"summary":"With a key","description":"GET /api/user/prefs","value":{"signedIn":true,"csrf":"6a1f…","copyHandleOnly":false,"saveRecentSearches":true}},"signed-out":{"summary":"Signed out","description":"GET /api/user/prefs","value":{"signedIn":false,"csrf":null,"copyHandleOnly":null,"saveRecentSearches":null}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{},{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"optional","x-rate-limit":null,"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false},"patch":{"operationId":"updatePrefs","tags":["Your account"],"summary":"Change your preferences","description":"Changes the preferences sent, each on its own; the others stay as they are. The body may be at most 1 KiB.","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"description":"The preferences to change.","required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PrefsChange"},"example":{"copyHandleOnly":true}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Changed.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"ok":{"type":"boolean","const":true}},"required":["ok"],"additionalProperties":false},"examples":{"copy":{"summary":"Copy handles bare","description":"PATCH /api/user/prefs","value":{"ok":true}}}}}},"400":{"description":"The body is not JSON, names no preference, or gives one the wrong type. Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["bad_json","bad_value"],"description":"`bad_json`: the body is not JSON. `bad_value`: no preference, or one of the wrong type."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]},"examples":{"bad":{"summary":"A value of the wrong type","description":"PATCH /api/user/prefs","value":{"error":"bad_value"}}}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"413":{"description":"The body is over 1 KiB.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["too_large"],"description":"The body is too large."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many changes in the last minute: counted per IP address, per account and per key (an admin key’s per key alone, at the limit set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":false,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"mutation"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/api/v1/entities/{vhid}":{"get":{"operationId":"getEntity","tags":["Entries"],"summary":"Get an entry","description":"Everything the entry’s page shows, as data: its title, description, images with their rights, and handles. It is built by the same code as the page, so the two never disagree. An old name or a merged entry’s key answers with the entry it now leads to, without a redirect; `vhid` and `url` say which entry that is. The same body is served at `/{key}.json`.\n\nAny origin may read it: `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`, methods GET and OPTIONS, no credentials. An `OPTIONS` preflight answers 204. No key is needed. A request that sends one (`Authorization: Bearer`) has it checked, so a wrong, revoked or expired key is refused 401, and is counted against the key’s read limit; it gets the same answer, marked `no-store`.","parameters":[{"name":"vhid","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The entry’s VHID (11 digits), its short name, or one of its old names. Short names are matched exactly.","schema":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":255},"example":"53500361835"}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The entry.","headers":{"ETag":{"description":"The version of this representation.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Entity"},"examples":{"byShort":{"summary":"An entry by its short name","description":"GET /api/v1/entities/james","value":{"vhid":"53500361835","short":"james","title":"James Haworth","subtitle":null,"entity_type":"person","entity_kind":"person","verified":true,"description":null,"description_source":null,"description_license":null,"url":"https://verifiedhandles.org/james","image":"/img/w/480q75/3","image_rights":{"source":"upload","license":null,"license_name":null,"license_url":null,"freely_licensed":null,"credit":null,"source_page":null,"details_url":"https://verifiedhandles.org/james/image"},"images":[{"url":"/img/w/480q75/3","main":true,"image_rights":{"source":"upload","license":null,"license_name":null,"license_url":null,"freely_licensed":null,"credit":null,"source_page":null,"details_url":"https://verifiedhandles.org/james/image"},"link":null}],"handles":[{"platform":"twitter","name":"X (Twitter)","category":"social","value":"james","display":null,"url":"https://x.com/james","verified":false},{"platform":"linkedin","name":"LinkedIn","category":"social","value":"james-haworth","display":null,"url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/james-haworth","verified":false},{"platform":"instagram","name":"Instagram","category":"social","value":"jameshaworth","display":null,"url":"https://instagram.com/jameshaworth","verified":false},{"platform":"email","name":"Email","category":"messaging","value":null,"display":null,"url":null,"verified":false}]}}}}}},"304":{"description":"Unchanged since the ETag sent in `If-None-Match`. No body."},"404":{"description":"No public entry answers to that key.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/NotFound"},"examples":{"notFound":{"summary":"A key nothing answers to","description":"GET /api/v1/entities/no-such-entry","value":{"error":"not_found"}}}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many requests from this IP address in the last minute (at a route that takes a key, an admin key’s are counted per key instead, at the limits set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"ignored","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"json","max":120,"window_seconds":60,"per":"IP address"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"public, max-age=60, s-maxage=2592000, stale-while-revalidate=86400, stale-if-error=604800","surrogate-keys":["entity:<vhid>"],"etag":true,"notes":"Shared caches may keep it for 30 days; an edit to the entry purges it at once (by its `entity:<vhid>` surrogate key). Browsers keep it for a minute. A strong ETag: send it back as `If-None-Match` and an unchanged entry answers 304, with no body."},"x-cors":true}},"/api/v1/entities":{"get":{"operationId":"getEntities","tags":["Entries"],"summary":"Get many entries at once","description":"Up to 50 entries in one request: the batch form of `GET /api/v1/entities/{vhid}`. Each key is answered exactly as that route answers it, in the order asked: the entry (`status: \"ok\"`, the same body), or `status: \"not_found\"` where it would answer 404. A deleted entry and a key that names nothing look the same. An old name or a merged entry’s key answers with the entry it now leads to; `entity.vhid` says which. A key repeated is answered once. The answer is 200 whatever each key answers: only the request itself is refused. A Wikidata QID is not a key here, as it is not at the single read: `GET /api/v1/search?q=Q42` finds the entries linked to an item. A key that contains a comma (only an old name can) cannot be asked for in a batch: use the single read.\n\n**Rate limit.** Each key counts as one read against the IP address’s budget, so 50 keys cost what 50 single reads cost, and the request is refused (429) when the budget cannot cover it. A response the edge already holds costs nothing.\n\nAny origin may read it: `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`, methods GET and OPTIONS, no credentials. An `OPTIONS` preflight answers 204. No key is needed. A request that sends one (`Authorization: Bearer`) has it checked, so a wrong, revoked or expired key is refused 401, and is counted against the key’s read limit; it gets the same answer, marked `no-store`.","parameters":[{"name":"ids","in":"query","required":true,"description":"The keys, comma-separated: each a VHID, a short name or an old name, as `{vhid}` takes. Each is trimmed; empty ones are dropped and a repeat counts once. At most 50 keys and 4096 characters.","schema":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":4096},"example":"james,53500361835,Verified_Handles"}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Each key’s answer.","headers":{"ETag":{"description":"The version of this answer.","schema":{"type":"string"}},"Surrogate-Key":{"description":"Every answered entry’s key.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EntityBatch"},"examples":{"twoKeys":{"summary":"One entry by its short name and by its VHID: each key answered","description":"GET /api/v1/entities?ids=james,53500361835","value":{"results":[{"key":"james","status":"ok","entity":{"vhid":"53500361835","short":"james","title":"James Haworth","subtitle":null,"entity_type":"person","entity_kind":"person","verified":true,"description":null,"description_source":null,"description_license":null,"url":"https://verifiedhandles.org/james","image":"/img/w/480q75/3","image_rights":{"source":"upload","license":null,"license_name":null,"license_url":null,"freely_licensed":null,"credit":null,"source_page":null,"details_url":"https://verifiedhandles.org/james/image"},"images":[{"url":"/img/w/480q75/3","main":true,"image_rights":{"source":"upload","license":null,"license_name":null,"license_url":null,"freely_licensed":null,"credit":null,"source_page":null,"details_url":"https://verifiedhandles.org/james/image"},"link":null}],"handles":[{"platform":"twitter","name":"X (Twitter)","category":"social","value":"james","display":null,"url":"https://x.com/james","verified":false},{"platform":"linkedin","name":"LinkedIn","category":"social","value":"james-haworth","display":null,"url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/james-haworth","verified":false},{"platform":"instagram","name":"Instagram","category":"social","value":"jameshaworth","display":null,"url":"https://instagram.com/jameshaworth","verified":false},{"platform":"email","name":"Email","category":"messaging","value":null,"display":null,"url":null,"verified":false}]}},{"key":"53500361835","status":"ok","entity":{"vhid":"53500361835","short":"james","title":"James Haworth","subtitle":null,"entity_type":"person","entity_kind":"person","verified":true,"description":null,"description_source":null,"description_license":null,"url":"https://verifiedhandles.org/james","image":"/img/w/480q75/3","image_rights":{"source":"upload","license":null,"license_name":null,"license_url":null,"freely_licensed":null,"credit":null,"source_page":null,"details_url":"https://verifiedhandles.org/james/image"},"images":[{"url":"/img/w/480q75/3","main":true,"image_rights":{"source":"upload","license":null,"license_name":null,"license_url":null,"freely_licensed":null,"credit":null,"source_page":null,"details_url":"https://verifiedhandles.org/james/image"},"link":null}],"handles":[{"platform":"twitter","name":"X (Twitter)","category":"social","value":"james","display":null,"url":"https://x.com/james","verified":false},{"platform":"linkedin","name":"LinkedIn","category":"social","value":"james-haworth","display":null,"url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/james-haworth","verified":false},{"platform":"instagram","name":"Instagram","category":"social","value":"jameshaworth","display":null,"url":"https://instagram.com/jameshaworth","verified":false},{"platform":"email","name":"Email","category":"messaging","value":null,"display":null,"url":null,"verified":false}]}}]}}}}}},"304":{"description":"Unchanged since the ETag sent in `If-None-Match`. No body."},"400":{"description":"`ids_required`: no keys. `too_many_ids`: more than `max` keys after removing repeats. `ids_too_long`: `ids` is over `max` characters.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["ids_required"],"description":"No keys were given."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["too_many_ids","ids_too_long"],"description":"Too many keys, or too long a list."},"max":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"The limit that was passed."}},"required":["error","max"],"additionalProperties":false}]},"examples":{"tooMany":{"summary":"More keys than a batch takes","description":"GET /api/v1/entities?ids=k0,k1,k2,k3,k4,k5,k6,k7,k8,k9,k10,k11,k12,k13,k14,k15,k16,k17,k18,k19,k20,k21,k22,k23,k24,k25,k26,k27,k28,k29,k30,k31,k32,k33,k34,k35,k36,k37,k38,k39,k40,k41,k42,k43,k44,k45,k46,k47,k48,k49,k50","value":{"error":"too_many_ids","max":50}},"empty":{"summary":"No keys","description":"GET /api/v1/entities?ids=","value":{"error":"ids_required"}}}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many requests from this IP address in the last minute (at a route that takes a key, an admin key’s are counted per key instead, at the limits set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"ignored","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"json","max":120,"window_seconds":60,"per":"IP address"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"public, max-age=60, s-maxage=2592000, stale-while-revalidate=86400, stale-if-error=604800","surrogate-keys":["entity:<vhid>"],"etag":true,"notes":"When every key answers an entry, shared caches may keep it for 30 days, as the single read: it carries the `entity:<vhid>` surrogate key of every entry in it, so an edit to any one of them purges it at once. When any key answers `not_found`, it is `public, max-age=0, s-maxage=60, stale-while-revalidate=60` instead: a key that names nothing has nothing to be purged by when it starts to. A strong ETag, from every answer in it: send it back as `If-None-Match` and an unchanged batch answers 304, with no body. The keys are not reordered: the same keys in another order are another URL, cached apart, so ask in a stable order."},"x-cors":true}},"/api/v1/entities/{vhid}/handles":{"get":{"operationId":"getEntityHandles","tags":["Entries"],"summary":"Get an entry’s handles","description":"Just the entry’s handles, in the order its page shows them: the same list as `handles` in the entry. An email address is listed with its value, label and URL all null.\n\nAny origin may read it: `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`, methods GET and OPTIONS, no credentials. An `OPTIONS` preflight answers 204. No key is needed. A request that sends one (`Authorization: Bearer`) has it checked, so a wrong, revoked or expired key is refused 401, and is counted against the key’s read limit; it gets the same answer, marked `no-store`.","parameters":[{"name":"vhid","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The entry’s VHID (11 digits), its short name, or one of its old names. Short names are matched exactly.","schema":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":255},"example":"53500361835"}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The entry’s handles.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EntityHandles"},"examples":{"byVhid":{"summary":"An entry’s handles, by VHID","description":"GET /api/v1/entities/53500361835/handles","value":{"vhid":"53500361835","handles":[{"platform":"twitter","name":"X (Twitter)","category":"social","value":"james","display":null,"url":"https://x.com/james","verified":false},{"platform":"linkedin","name":"LinkedIn","category":"social","value":"james-haworth","display":null,"url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/james-haworth","verified":false},{"platform":"instagram","name":"Instagram","category":"social","value":"jameshaworth","display":null,"url":"https://instagram.com/jameshaworth","verified":false},{"platform":"email","name":"Email","category":"messaging","value":null,"display":null,"url":null,"verified":false}]}}}}}},"404":{"description":"No public entry answers to that key.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/NotFound"}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many requests from this IP address in the last minute (at a route that takes a key, an admin key’s are counted per key instead, at the limits set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"ignored","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"json","max":120,"window_seconds":60,"per":"IP address"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"public, max-age=60, s-maxage=2592000, stale-while-revalidate=86400, stale-if-error=604800","surrogate-keys":["entity:<vhid>"],"etag":false,"notes":"Shared caches may keep it for 30 days; an edit to the entry purges it at once (by its `entity:<vhid>` surrogate key). Browsers keep it for a minute."},"x-cors":true}},"/api/v1/entities/{vhid}/history":{"get":{"operationId":"getEntityHistory","tags":["History"],"summary":"Get an entry’s revision history","description":"The entry’s public revision history, newest first, a page at a time: the history kept from the old wiki and every edit made since. Hidden and deleted revisions are never listed, and an editor is named only if they chose to be. A merged entry’s key answers with that entry’s own history, and `merged_into` names the entry it became. An entry whose history has been hidden answers 404.\n\nAny origin may read it: `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`, methods GET and OPTIONS, no credentials. An `OPTIONS` preflight answers 204. No key is needed. A request that sends one (`Authorization: Bearer`) has it checked, so a wrong, revoked or expired key is refused 401, and is counted against the key’s read limit; it gets the same answer, marked `no-store`.","parameters":[{"name":"vhid","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The entry’s VHID (11 digits), its short name, or one of its old names. Short names are matched exactly.","schema":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":255},"example":"53500361835"},{"name":"limit","in":"query","required":false,"description":"How many revisions a page holds. Out of range is clamped; anything else non-numeric reads as the default.","schema":{"default":100,"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":200}},{"name":"offset","in":"query","required":false,"description":"How many revisions to skip. Clamped to 0–10,000.","schema":{"default":0,"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":10000}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"A page of the history.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EntityHistory"},"examples":{"firstPage":{"summary":"The first page, two revisions to a page","description":"GET /api/v1/entities/james/history?limit=2","value":{"vhid":"53500361835","limit":2,"offset":0,"next_offset":null,"history":[{"ref_id":"r1","kind":"forward","ts":"2026-09-19T12:00:00.000Z","actor":null,"summary":null,"is_bot":false,"source":"import","hidden":false,"deleted":false,"proposer":null}]}}}}}},"404":{"description":"No public entry answers to that key, or its history is hidden.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/NotFound"}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many requests from this IP address in the last minute (at a route that takes a key, an admin key’s are counted per key instead, at the limits set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"ignored","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"json","max":120,"window_seconds":60,"per":"IP address"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"public, max-age=0, s-maxage=300, stale-while-revalidate=300","surrogate-keys":["entity:<vhid>","entity:<merged_into>"],"etag":false,"notes":"Shared caches keep it for 5 minutes, and an edit purges it at once. Browsers revalidate on every request. A merged entry’s history also carries the surrogate key of the entry it was merged into."},"x-cors":true}},"/api/v1/search":{"get":{"operationId":"search","tags":["Search"],"summary":"Search the entries","description":"Full-text search over every public entry’s title, short name, subtitle and description, best match first. Two kinds of query are looked up instead of searched: a Wikidata QID (`Q42`) finds the entries linked to that item, and a VHID finds its entry and the entries that link to it. Each of those is one page: `offset` is ignored and `next_offset` is null.\n\nAny origin may read it: `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`, methods GET and OPTIONS, no credentials. An `OPTIONS` preflight answers 204. No key is needed. A request that sends one (`Authorization: Bearer`) has it checked, so a wrong, revoked or expired key is refused 401, and is counted against the key’s read limit; it gets the same answer, marked `no-store`.","parameters":[{"name":"q","in":"query","required":true,"description":"What to search for: words, a QID or a VHID. Trimmed and cut to 100 characters. Empty searches nothing.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"james"},{"name":"limit","in":"query","required":false,"description":"How many results a page holds. Out of range is clamped; anything else non-numeric reads as the default.","schema":{"default":20,"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":50}},{"name":"offset","in":"query","required":false,"description":"How many results to skip. Clamped to 0–10,000. Ignored for a QID or a VHID.","schema":{"default":0,"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":10000}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"A page of results; for an empty `q`, an empty answer with no paging fields.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/SearchResponse"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EmptySearch"}]},"examples":{"words":{"summary":"A search for a name","description":"GET /api/v1/search?q=james&limit=2","value":{"query":"james","total":1,"limit":2,"offset":0,"next_offset":null,"results":[{"vhid":"53500361835","short":"james","title":"James Haworth","subtitle":null,"verified":true,"snippet":null,"highlighted":false,"url":"https://verifiedhandles.org/james"}]}}}}}},"422":{"description":"The query is one of the phrases the site does not search for.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Blocked"},"examples":{"blocked":{"summary":"A query the site does not search for","description":"GET /api/v1/search?q=sadist","value":{"error":"blocked","query":"sadist"}}}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many requests from this IP address in the last minute (at a route that takes a key, an admin key’s are counted per key instead, at the limits set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"ignored","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"json","max":120,"window_seconds":60,"per":"IP address"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"public, max-age=0, s-maxage=60, stale-while-revalidate=60","surrogate-keys":["listing"],"etag":false,"notes":"Shared caches keep a result for a minute; blocking or unblocking an entry purges every result at once (the `listing` surrogate key). An empty query is not cached at all, nor is a refused one."},"x-cors":true}},"/api/v1/handles":{"get":{"operationId":"findByHandle","tags":["Entries"],"summary":"Find the entries that list a handle","description":"Which public entries list this handle: “is x.com/someone an official account, and whose?”. Ask by `platform` and `value`, or by `url`, a profile’s address, which is read as the editor reads a pasted one: the platform whose address it is, and what follows it (`https://x.com/someone?s=20` is `twitter`, `someone`). The value is matched as the site stores and compares a handle: trimmed, case ignored on a platform that ignores it, a leading `@` optional on a platform shown with one, and a website completed to its `https://` address. An entry that lists the handle twice (`@x` and `x`) is answered once. A deleted entry, and a handle on a platform the site does not show, are never answered, nor is a Facebook value that is one of Facebook’s own path words (`pg`, `groups`, `?fref=ts`: no one’s account, and not shown on any entry). Email addresses are not looked up. Nothing found is a 200 with an empty `results`.\n\nAny origin may read it: `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`, methods GET and OPTIONS, no credentials. An `OPTIONS` preflight answers 204. No key is needed. A request that sends one (`Authorization: Bearer`) has it checked, so a wrong, revoked or expired key is refused 401, and is counted against the key’s read limit; it gets the same answer, marked `no-store`.","parameters":[{"name":"platform","in":"query","required":false,"description":"The platform’s id in the catalog (`twitter`, `instagram`, `youtube`, …). With `value`; not with `url`.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"twitter"},{"name":"value","in":"query","required":false,"description":"The handle, as it follows the platform’s address (`someone` or `@someone`). At most 1,000 characters.","schema":{"type":"string","maxLength":1000},"example":"james"},{"name":"url","in":"query","required":false,"description":"A profile’s address, instead of `platform` and `value`: `https://x.com/someone`. The scheme is optional; the query, the fragment and trailing slashes are ignored. At most 1,000 characters.","schema":{"type":"string","maxLength":1000},"example":"https://x.com/james"}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The entries that list the handle, perhaps none.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HandleLookupResponse"},"examples":{"byValue":{"summary":"A handle by platform and value, in another case and with its @","description":"GET /api/v1/handles?platform=twitter&value=@James","value":{"platform":"twitter","value":"James","results":[{"vhid":"53500361835","title":"James Haworth","url":"https://verifiedhandles.org/james","value":"james","verified":false}]}},"byUrl":{"summary":"The same handle by its profile’s address","description":"GET /api/v1/handles?url=https://x.com/james?s=20","value":{"platform":"twitter","value":"james","results":[{"vhid":"53500361835","title":"James Haworth","url":"https://verifiedhandles.org/james","value":"james","verified":false}]}},"none":{"summary":"A handle no entry lists","description":"GET /api/v1/handles?platform=twitter&value=nobody-lists-this","value":{"platform":"twitter","value":"nobody-lists-this","results":[]}}}}}},"400":{"description":"`platform_required`: neither a platform nor a url. `url_or_platform`: both. `unknown_platform`: not a platform the site lists handles on; `platforms` lists the ones it does. `masked_platform`: `email`. `value_required`, `value_too_long`. `url_not_recognised`: no platform’s address is that one. Each with a `message` saying so.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["platform_required","url_or_platform","unknown_platform","masked_platform","value_required","value_too_long","url_not_recognised"],"description":"What is wrong with the request."},"message":{"type":"string","description":"The same, in words."},"platforms":{"description":"With `unknown_platform`: the platform ids a look-up takes.","type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["error","message"],"additionalProperties":false},"examples":{"unknownPlatform":{"summary":"A platform the site does not list","description":"GET /api/v1/handles?platform=myspace&value=tom","value":{"error":"unknown_platform","message":"\"myspace\" is not a platform the site lists handles on. `platforms` lists the ones it does.","platforms":["twitter"]}}}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many requests from this IP address in the last minute (at a route that takes a key, an admin key’s are counted per key instead, at the limits set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"ignored","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"json","max":120,"window_seconds":60,"per":"IP address"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"public, max-age=0, s-maxage=60, stale-while-revalidate=60","surrogate-keys":["listing","entity:<vhid>"],"etag":false,"notes":"Shared caches keep an answer for a minute, as search: an edit to an entry it lists purges it at once (each entry’s `entity:<vhid>` surrogate key), as does blocking or unblocking any entry (`listing`). An entry that adds the handle shows within the minute. A refused request is not cached."},"x-cors":true}},"/api/v1/openapi.json":{"get":{"operationId":"getOpenApi","tags":["About the API"],"summary":"Get this document","description":"This description of the public API, as OpenAPI 3.1. It is generated from the same registry the routes are tested against, so it changes when the API does.\n\nAny origin may read it: `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`, methods GET and OPTIONS, no credentials. An `OPTIONS` preflight answers 204. No key is needed. A request that sends one (`Authorization: Bearer`) has it checked, so a wrong, revoked or expired key is refused 401, and is counted against the key’s read limit; it gets the same answer, marked `no-store`.","parameters":[],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The OpenAPI document.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/OpenApiDocument"}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many requests from this IP address in the last minute (at a route that takes a key, an admin key’s are counted per key instead, at the limits set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"ignored","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"json","max":120,"window_seconds":60,"per":"IP address"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"public, max-age=3600","etag":false,"notes":"Anyone may keep it for an hour."},"x-cors":true}},"/api/wikidata/items/{qid}":{"get":{"operationId":"getWikidataItem","tags":["Proposing changes"],"summary":"Read a Wikidata item","description":"What a Wikidata item says, the way the Wikidata sync would store it: label, description, image and handles, with the entries already on it. For proposing what it says onto an entry. It asks Wikidata within a lookup budget per account and for the site, behind a short cache; over budget, or when Wikidata does not answer, a 503: try again in a minute.","parameters":[{"name":"qid","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The item, `Q<n>`.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"Q42"}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The item.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/WikidataItem"},"examples":{"q42":{"summary":"An item","description":"GET /api/wikidata/items/Q42","value":{"qid":"Q42","label":"Douglas Adams","description":"English author and humourist (1952–2001)","image":{"filename":"Douglas adams portrait cropped.jpg","token":"eyJ…"},"handles":[{"platform_id":"website","value":"https://douglasadams.com/","value_norm":"https://douglasadams.com/"}],"entries_on_item":[]}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Not a QID (`bad_qid`). Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["bad_qid"],"description":"Not a QID."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]},"examples":{"bad":{"summary":"Not a QID","description":"GET /api/wikidata/items/42x","value":{"error":"bad_qid"}}}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"The account may not propose (`forbidden`). A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"404":{"description":"Wikidata has no such item.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","const":"wikidata_no_item"},"qid":{"type":"string"}},"required":["error","qid"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many changes in the last minute: counted per IP address, per account and per key (an admin key’s per key alone, at the limit set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"Over the lookup budget, or Wikidata did not answer (JSON, with `Retry-After: 60`); or the site is down for maintenance (an HTML page).","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","const":"wikidata_busy"},"retry":{"type":"boolean","const":true}},"required":["error","retry"],"additionalProperties":false}}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":"propose","x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"mutation"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/applications/check.json":{"get":{"operationId":"checkApplication","tags":["Applying for an entry"],"summary":"Check for an entry before applying","description":"Whether the site already has the entry you would apply for: the entry on a Wikidata item, and up to 5 entries whose names match a title. It reads only this site, never Wikidata.","parameters":[{"name":"qid","in":"query","required":false,"description":"A Wikidata item, `Q<n>`.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"Q7259"},{"name":"title","in":"query","required":false,"description":"A name. Fewer than 2 characters matches nothing; cut to 100.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"james"}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"What the site has.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApplicationCheck"},"examples":{"james":{"summary":"By a name","description":"GET /applications/check.json?title=james","value":{"qid":null,"title":[{"vhid":"53500361835","title":"James Haworth","short":"james"}]}}}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many requests from this IP address in the last minute (at a route that takes a key, an admin key’s are counted per key instead, at the limits set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{},{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"optional","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"json","max":120,"window_seconds":60,"per":"IP address"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached, so an entry made a moment ago is found."},"x-cors":false}},"/applications/wikidata.json":{"get":{"operationId":"suggestFromWikidata","tags":["Applying for an entry"],"summary":"Find the Wikidata item to apply with","description":"Up to 6 Wikidata items whose names match, each with the entry already on it. It asks Wikidata, within a lookup budget per account and for the site; past the budget, or when Wikidata does not answer, `status` is `unavailable`. Fewer than 2 characters answers no items.","parameters":[{"name":"q","in":"query","required":true,"description":"A name.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"Ada Lovelace"}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The items, or `unavailable`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","const":"ok"},"hits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"qid":{"type":"string"},"label":{"type":"string"},"description":{"type":"string"},"entry":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"vhid":{"type":"string"},"short":{"type":["string","null"]},"title":{"type":"string"}},"required":["vhid","short","title"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The entry already on the item, or null."}},"required":["qid","label","description","entry"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"required":["status","hits"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","const":"unavailable"}},"required":["status"],"additionalProperties":false}]},"examples":{"short":{"summary":"Too short to look up","description":"GET /applications/wikidata.json?q=a","value":{"status":"ok","hits":[]}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many requests from this IP address in the last minute (at a route that takes a key, an admin key’s are counted per key instead, at the limits set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"json","max":120,"window_seconds":60,"per":"IP address"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/applications":{"post":{"operationId":"applyForEntry","tags":["Applying for an entry"],"summary":"Apply for an entry","description":"Files an application, which a reviewer decides; you are told by email, and can follow it at `/applications/{id}`. Check first with `GET /applications/check.json`: an item already on an entry is refused, as is an item Wikidata has merged into another (the message names the item it kept), and asking again about one you already have open answers that one (`?dup=1`). 10 a day. A refusal is the form again, as HTML, with every value kept and each problem beside its field.","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"description":"The application.","required":true,"content":{"application/x-www-form-urlencoded":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApplicationForm"},"example":{"title":"Api Docs Application","relationship":"self","handle_platform":"twitter","handle_value":"apidocsapp","wikipedia_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Test","consent":"1"}}}},"responses":{"303":{"description":"Filed: on to it, `?sent=1`. Or you already have one open on that subject: on to that one, `?dup=1`.","headers":{"Location":{"description":"`/applications/<id>?sent=1`, or `?dup=1`.","schema":{"type":"string"}}}},"400":{"description":"The form again, as HTML, with what to fix. (A key with a cookie: `bearer_with_cookie`, JSON.)","content":{"text/html":{}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"Your account may not propose: a page that says so. (A read-only key, or a blocked account: JSON.)","content":{"text/html":{}}},"429":{"description":"10 applications in the last day already: the form again, saying so. Or too many changes in the last minute, as text, with `Retry-After`.","content":{"text/html":{}}},"503":{"description":"Applications are paused: a page that says so.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":"propose","x-read-only-key":false,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":null,"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/applications/{id}/comments":{"post":{"operationId":"replyToMyApplication","tags":["Applying for an entry"],"summary":"Reply on your application","description":"Adds to the application’s conversation with its reviewers; a reply to a question (`needs_info`) puts it back in their queue. Back to the application, or `?error=<why>` (`empty`, `blocked` for blocked language, `closed` once it is decided).","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The application’s id.","schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\d+$"},"example":"990000001"}],"requestBody":{"description":"The reply.","required":true,"content":{"application/x-www-form-urlencoded":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"body":{"type":"string","description":"What to say, up to 2,000 characters."}},"required":["body"],"additionalProperties":false},"example":{"body":"The Wikipedia article was updated this week."}}}},"responses":{"303":{"description":"Back to the application’s conversation.","headers":{"Location":{"description":"`/applications/<id>#vh-thread-h`, or with `?error=<why>`.","schema":{"type":"string"}}}},"400":{"description":"Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"404":{"description":"No such application, or not yours: the not-found page.","content":{"text/html":{}}},"429":{"description":"Too many changes in the last minute: counted per IP address, per account and per key (an admin key’s per key alone, at the limit set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":false,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":null,"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/applications/{id}/retract":{"post":{"operationId":"retractMyApplication","tags":["Applying for an entry"],"summary":"Withdraw your application","description":"Withdraws it while it is still open. Back to the application, or `?error=cannot_retract` once it is decided.","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The application’s id.","schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\d+$"},"example":"990000001"}],"requestBody":{"description":"Nothing: the address says which.","required":true,"content":{"application/x-www-form-urlencoded":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false},"example":{}}}},"responses":{"303":{"description":"Back to the application.","headers":{"Location":{"description":"`/applications/<id>`, or with `?error=cannot_retract`.","schema":{"type":"string"}}}},"400":{"description":"Or the request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}}}},"401":{"description":"No key was sent (`auth_required`), or the key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. After 60 refused keys from one IP address in a minute, every key from there is answered `429` (text, with `Retry-After`) until the minute is up.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AuthRequired"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"403":{"description":"A read-only key tried to change something (`read_only_key`), or the account is blocked (`forbidden`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Forbidden"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}]}}}},"404":{"description":"No such application, or not yours: the not-found page.","content":{"text/html":{}}},"429":{"description":"Too many changes in the last minute: counted per IP address, per account and per key (an admin key’s per key alone, at the limit set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":false,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":null,"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/management-console/find":{"get":{"operationId":"consoleFindEntry","tags":["Entry manager"],"summary":"Find an entry by name, for a console form or the console search","description":"Up to 10 entries matching `find`: blocked ones too for an account with `manage_entries` or `suppress_history`, else what the public search finds. Each says whether its history is hidden and, to an account that may open its Wikidata page, whether the sync may read it now (linked to an item, neither protected nor claimed; false to anyone else): what the console search needs to offer the entry’s other pages. Empty `find`: none.","parameters":[{"name":"find","in":"query","required":false,"description":"Words in the title or short name, a VHID or a QID.","schema":{"type":"string"},"example":"James"}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The matches.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"VHID":{"type":"string"},"Title":{"type":"string"},"short":{"type":["string","null"]},"blocked":{"type":"boolean"},"history_hidden":{"type":"boolean"},"syncable":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["VHID","Title","short","blocked","history_hidden","syncable"],"additionalProperties":false}},"examples":{"empty":{"summary":"Nothing asked","description":"GET /management-console/find","value":[]}}}}},"302":{"description":"No key was sent: the console sends a browser to sign in. A script should send its key.","headers":{"Location":{"description":"/management-console/auth/login?next=<the path asked for>","schema":{"type":"string"}}}},"400":{"description":"The request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}}}},"401":{"description":"The key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key’s account lacks the capability, or is blocked: the body is the word `Forbidden`.","content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Forbidden"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":null,"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/management-console/submissions.json":{"get":{"operationId":"listMySubmissions","tags":["Your account"],"summary":"List what you have sent for review","description":"Your proposals, new entries, claims, reports and applications, newest first, 25 to a page: every one, or with `status=open` only those still waiting on a decision.","parameters":[{"name":"status","in":"query","required":false,"description":"`open`: only those waiting on a decision. Anything else: all of them.","schema":{"default":"all","type":"string","enum":["open","all"]}},{"name":"page","in":"query","required":false,"description":"The page, from 1; past 10,000 it is clamped.","schema":{"default":1,"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":10000}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"A page of your submissions.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["open","all"]},"page":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":9007199254740991},"per_page":{"type":"number","const":25},"total":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991},"has_next":{"type":"boolean"},"submissions":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/SubmissionBrief"}}},"required":["status","page","per_page","total","has_next","submissions"],"additionalProperties":false},"examples":{"open":{"summary":"Those still waiting","description":"GET /management-console/submissions.json?status=open","value":{"status":"open","page":1,"per_page":25,"total":1,"has_next":false,"submissions":[{"id":"990000002","kind":"new_entity","status":"pending","entry":null,"qid":null,"created_at":"2026-10-05T12:00:00.000Z","decided_at":null,"review_notes":null}]}}}}}},"302":{"description":"No key was sent: the console sends a browser to sign in. A script should send its key.","headers":{"Location":{"description":"/management-console/auth/login?next=<the path asked for>","schema":{"type":"string"}}}},"400":{"description":"The request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}}}},"401":{"description":"The key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key’s account lacks the capability, or is blocked: the body is the word `Forbidden`.","content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Forbidden"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"json","max":120,"window_seconds":60,"per":"IP address"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/management-console/submissions/{file}":{"get":{"operationId":"getMySubmission","tags":["Your account"],"summary":"Read one of your submissions, with its conversation","description":"One submission, what it asked for (`payload`, as it was sent) and its comments, oldest first. Its submitter and reviewers may read it; to anyone else it is 404, as a missing one is. A masked email the proposal keeps is in `payload.handles` as `{value: '', kept: true, ref}`, never its address; one it removes is left out. Its page shows such a removal as “Email: (an address)” to a submitter who may not edit the entry live.","parameters":[{"name":"file","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The submission’s id, then `.json`.","schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\d{1,18}\\.json$"},"example":"990000002.json"}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The submission.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/SubmissionDetail"},"examples":{"mine":{"summary":"A new entry you proposed","description":"GET /management-console/submissions/990000002.json","value":{"id":"990000002","kind":"new_entity","status":"pending","entry":null,"qid":null,"created_at":"2026-10-05T12:00:00.000Z","decided_at":null,"review_notes":null,"mine":true,"payload":{"title":"Api Docs Proposal","handles":[]},"comments":[]}}}}}},"302":{"description":"No key was sent: the console sends a browser to sign in. A script should send its key.","headers":{"Location":{"description":"/management-console/auth/login?next=<the path asked for>","schema":{"type":"string"}}}},"400":{"description":"The request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}}}},"401":{"description":"The key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key’s account lacks the capability, or is blocked: the body is the word `Forbidden`.","content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Forbidden"}}}},"404":{"description":"No such submission, or not one you may read.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["not_found"],"description":"Not found."}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":{}},"examples":{"missing":{"summary":"Not there","description":"GET /management-console/submissions/999999999.json","value":{"error":"not_found"}}}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":true,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":{"bucket":"json","max":120,"window_seconds":60,"per":"IP address"},"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the caller. An answer to a key also carries `Vary: Authorization`."},"x-cors":false}},"/management-console/submissions/{id}/comments":{"post":{"operationId":"commentOnMySubmission","tags":["Your account"],"summary":"Comment on one of your submissions","description":"Adds a comment to the submission’s conversation, which its reviewers read. Answers as the page’s form does: back to the submission, `done=commented`, or `error=<why>` (`empty`, `blocked` for blocked language, `closed` once it is decided).","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The submission’s id.","schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\d+$"},"example":"990000002"}],"requestBody":{"description":"The comment.","required":true,"content":{"application/x-www-form-urlencoded":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"body":{"type":"string","description":"What to say, up to 2,000 characters."}},"required":["body"],"additionalProperties":false},"example":{"body":"The handles are on the subject’s own website."}}}},"responses":{"302":{"description":"No key was sent: the console sends a browser to sign in. A script should send its key.","headers":{"Location":{"description":"/management-console/auth/login?next=<the path asked for>","schema":{"type":"string"}}}},"303":{"description":"Done: back to /management-console/submissions/<id>, `done=commented` or `error=<why>`.","headers":{"Location":{"description":"/management-console/submissions/<id>, with the outcome in its query.","schema":{"type":"string"}}}},"400":{"description":"The request sent a key and a session cookie together (`bearer_with_cookie`): send one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}}}},"401":{"description":"The key was refused: unknown, revoked or expired, its holder may no longer use keys, or this instance takes none. Carries `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKeyRefusal"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key’s account lacks the capability, or is blocked: the body is the word `Forbidden`. A read-only key that tries to change something is refused first, as JSON: `{\"error\":\"read_only_key\"}`.","content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Forbidden"}}}},"404":{"description":"No such submission, or not one you may comment on.","content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string"}}}},"429":{"description":"Too many changes in the last minute: counted per IP address, per account and per key (an admin key’s per key alone, at the limit set on Console → Rate limits). Wait the number of seconds `Retry-After` gives.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds until the window resets.","schema":{"type":"string"}}},"content":{"text/plain":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"Too Many Requests"}}}},"503":{"description":"The site is down for maintenance. The body is the maintenance page, as HTML. Try again later: `Retry-After` gives the seconds.","content":{"text/html":{}}}},"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"x-audience":"public","x-capability":null,"x-read-only-key":false,"x-auth":"required","x-rate-limit":null,"x-cache":{"cache-control":"no-store","etag":false,"notes":"Never cached: it is about the 