wn beside it."}},"additionalProperties":{},"description":"A dry run (`dry_run: true`): what the change would be and the exact request it would send. A real run: what the route answered."}},{"name":"set_entry_image","title":"Set or clear an entry’s image","description":"Put an image on an entry — one already on the site (`media_id`, from media_catalog or get_entry) or a Wikimedia Commons file (`commons_token`, from search_commons_images) — or take the image off (`clear: true`). A new image starts with no link; `link` sets the address the image opens on the entry page instead of the full-screen viewer (`\"\"` clears it), which needs Link images. A live edit, audited. Setting the image yourself takes it from the Wikidata sync. Dry run by default. To ask a reviewer instead, use propose_entry_change.","write":true,"confirm":false,"capabilities":[],"role":null,"keyless":false,"liveEdit":true,"linkImages":true,"input":{"type":"object","properties":{"entry":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"pattern":"^(?!\\.{1,2}$)","description":"The entry: its VHID (11 digits), its short name (as in verifiedhandles.org/<short>), or its Wikidata QID (Q42)."},"media_id":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]{1,18}$"},"commons_token":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2000},"clear":{"type":"boolean"},"link":{"description":"An absolute https:// (or http://) address the image links to instead of opening the full-screen viewer; \"\" for no link. Needs Link images.","type":"string","maxLength":2048},"summary":{"description":"Why you made this edit, in a few plain words; shown in the entry’s public history. At most 200 characters. Never an internal tracking ID (a backlog or ticket number); a VHID is fine.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"base_revision_id":{"description":"The revision you read (get_entry → editing.baseRevisionId). If the entry has changed since, the edit is refused as a conflict. Left out, the current revision is used.","type":"string","pattern":"