mage: the whole ordered list of media ids (from media_catalog or get_entry), replacing the gallery; [] empties it. At most 5 (6 images in all with the lead), each once, never the lead itself (set_entry_image sets that). An image taken off loses its link; `links` sets or clears the link of an image in the list (needs Link images). A live edit, audited. Dry run by default. To ask a reviewer instead, use propose_entry_change.","write":true,"confirm":false,"capabilities":[],"role":null,"keyless":false,"liveEdit":true,"linkImages":true,"input":{"type":"object","properties":{"entry":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"pattern":"^(?!\\.{1,2}$)","description":"The entry: its VHID (11 digits), its short name (as in verifiedhandles.org/<short>), or its Wikidata QID (Q42)."},"media_ids":{"maxItems":50,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]{1,18}$"}},"links":{"description":"media id → the address that image links to on the entry page instead of the full-screen viewer; \"\" clears it. Images not named keep theirs. Needs Link images.","type":"object","propertyNames":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]{1,18}$"},"additionalProperties":{"type":"string","maxLength":2048}},"summary":{"description":"Why you made this edit, in a few plain words; shown in the entry’s public history. At most 200 characters. Never an internal tracking ID (a backlog or ticket number); a VHID is fine.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"base_revision_id":{"description":"The revision you read (get_entry → editing.baseRevisionId). If the entry has changed since, the edit is refused as a conflict. Left out, the current revision is used.","type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]+$"},"idempotency_key":{"description":"Optional: a key you choose (1–255 printable ASCII, e.g. a UUID), sent as the write’s Idempotency-Key. Calling again with the same key and the same change within 24 hours answers the first call’s result (replayed: true) and writes nothing; the same key with another change is refused (422).","type":"string","pattern":"^[\\x20-\\x7E]{1,255}$"},"dry_run":{"default":true,"description":"true (the default): write nothing — show the change and the exact request it would send. false: make the change.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["entry","media_ids"]},"output":{"type":"object","properties":{"dry_run":{"description":"true: a dry run, which wrote nothing. Absent from a real run.","type":"boolean"},"would_send":{"description":"A dry run: the exact request the real run would send (`method`, `path`, any `headers` such as an Idempotency-Key, and its `body`, `form` or `query`), or the requests, in order."},"note":{"description":"A dry run: what to do next to make the change, in words."},"confirm":{"description":"A dry run of a change that needs it: the exact target to send back as `confirm` with dry_run: false.","type":"string"},"replayed":{"description":"A real run with an idempotency_key already used for this change: the first call’s answer, given back; nothing was written now.","type":"boolean","const":true},"may_edit_live":{"description":"A dry run of a live edit: whether this key’s account may edit this entry live.","type":"boolean"},"refused_because":{"description":"A dry run the real run would be refused for: why, in words.","type":"string"},"result":{"description":"A real run: the route’s own answer, where the tool adds facts of its own beside it."}},"additionalProperties":{},"description":"A dry run (`dry_run: true`): what the change would be and the exact request it would send. A real run: what the route answered."}},{"name":"propose_entry_revert","title":"Propose putting an entry back to an earlier revision","description":"Propose, for a reviewer to decide, putting an entry back as it was at one of its revisions (get_entry_history: a `ref_id` like \"r123\"; imported legacy revisions cannot be put back). The proposal holds only what differs from now — title, subtitle, description, short name, handles and their order, lead image, gallery — as propose_entry_change would send it; who manages each value (Wikidata or the site) is left as it is. An image withdrawn since is left out, and the answer names it. Refused (nothing_to_change) when the entry already matches that revision. `note` tells the reviewer why. Audited. Dry run by default.","write":true,"confirm":false,"capabilities":["propose"],"role":null,"keyless":false,"liveEdit":false,"linkImages":false,"input":{"type":"object","properties":{"entry":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"pattern":"^(?!\\.{1,2}$)","description":"The entry: its VHID (11 digits), its short name (as in verifiedhandles.org/<short>), or its Wikidata QID (Q42)."},"revision":{"type":"string","pattern":"^r[0-9]+$","description":"The revision’s ref_id, e.g. \"r123\"."},"note":{"description":"Why you propose this, in plain words: posted as the proposal’s first comment, which the reviewer reads with it. At most 2,000 characters. Never an internal tracking ID (a backlog or ticket number); a VHID is fine.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2000},"idempotency_key":{"description":"Optional: a key you choose (1–255 printable ASCII, e.g. a UUID), sent as the write’s Idempotency-Key. Calling again with the same key and the same change within 24 hours answers the first call’s result (replayed: true) and writes nothing; the same key with another change is refused (422).","type":"string","pattern":"^[\\x20-\\x7E]{1,255}$"},"dry_run":{"default":true,"description":"true (the default): write nothing — show the change and the exact request it would send. false: make the change.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["entry","revision"]},"output":{"type":"object","properties":{"dry_run":{"description":"true: a dry run, which wrote nothing. Absent from a real run.","type":"boolean"},"would_send":{"description":"A dry run: the exact request the real run would send (`method`, `path`, any `headers` such as an Idempotency-Key, and its `body`, `form` or `query`), or the requests, in order."},"note":{"description":"A dry run: what to do next to make the change, in words."},"confirm":{"description":"A dry run of a change that needs it: the exact target to send back as `confirm` with dry_run: false.","type":"string"},"replayed":{"description":"A real run with an idempotency_key already used for this change: the first call’s answer, given back; nothing was written now.","type":"boolean","const":true},"may_edit_live":{"description":"A dry run of a live edit: whether this key’s account may edit this entry live.","type":"boolean"},"refused_because":{"description":"A dry run the real run would be refused for: why, in words.","type":"string"},"result":{"description":"A real run: the route’s own answer, where the tool adds facts of its own beside it."}},"additionalProperties":{},"description":"A dry run (`dry_run: true`): what the change would be and the exact request it would send. A real run: what the route answered."}},{"name":"propose_entry_change","title":"Propose a change to an entry","description":"Propose a change for a reviewer to decide — for any entry you may propose to, including ones you could edit live; nothing changes until a person approves it. Give only what changes; null clears a field. `qid` proposes linking the entry to a Wikidata item, or a different one (null: unlink it), with `adopt` naming the fields the item may manage (left out: the server’s default on a first link, unchanged on a re-point); only a reviewer with Manage entries may approve that. `note` tells the reviewer why. Audited. Dry run by default: it names the entries already on the item.","write":true,"confirm":false,"capabilities":["propose"],"role":null,"keyless":false,"liveEdit":false,"linkImages":false,"input":{"type":"object","properties":{"entry":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"pattern":"^(?!\\.{1,2}$)","description":"The entry: its VHID (11 digits), its short name (as in verifiedhandles.org/<short>), or its Wikidata QID (Q42)."},"title":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":500},"subtitle":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":500},{"type":"null"}]},"description":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":65536},{"type":"null"}]},"short":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":100},{"type":"null"}]},"remove_wikipedia_credit":{"description":"true: remove the “from Wikipedia” credit from the description.","type":"boolean"},"credit_wikipedia_page":{"description":"Credit the description “from Wikipedia”: an English Wikipedia article or draft, by title (\"Draft:Dominic McLaughlin\") or address. The server reads the page (redirects followed) and refuses it unless at least half of the description’s three-word phrases are the page’s lead (credit_text_differs, with the share).","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2000},"credit_let_wikidata_manage":{"description":"With a draft named in credit_wikipedia_page: false keeps the description site-authored. By default a draft’s credit hands the description to the Wikidata sync, which leaves it alone until the draft is an article linked from the entry’s Wikidata item.","type":"boolean"},"add_handles":{"maxItems":50,"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"platform_id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The platform id, e.g. \"twitter\": one the platform catalog has (get_entry with include_platforms lists the enabled ones; platform_catalog, every one). A new handle on an unknown or disabled platform is refused (400 invalid_platform)."},"value":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The handle as stored, e.g. \"nasa\"."},"display":{"type":"string","maxLength":200}},"required":["platform_id","value"]}},"remove_handles":{"description":"Handles to take off, each by its value — or, for an email this key may not see (value null in get_entry’s editing.handles), by {platform_id: \"email\", ref}.","maxItems":50,"type":"array","items":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"platform_id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The platform id, e.g. \"twitter\": one the platform catalog has (get_entry with include_platforms lists the enabled ones; platform_catalog, every one). A new handle on an unknown or disabled platform is refused (400 invalid_platform)."},"value":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The handle as stored, e.g. \"nasa\"."}},"required":["platform_id","value"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"platform_id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The masked handle’s platform: \"email\"."},"ref":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]{1,18}$","description":"A masked handle’s `ref` (get_entry → editing.handles, where its value is null): it names the stored handle without its address."}},"required":["platform_id","ref"]}]}},"handle_order":{"description":"Every handle, in the order the entry should show them: exactly the entry’s handles after add_handles and remove_handles, each once (a masked email by its ref).","maxItems":100,"type":"array","items":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"platform_id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The platform id, e.g. \"twitter\": one the platform catalog has (get_entry with include_platforms lists the enabled ones; platform_catalog, every one). A new handle on an unknown or disabled platform is refused (400 invalid_platform)."},"value":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The handle as stored, e.g. \"nasa\"."}},"required":["platform_id","value"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"platform_id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The masked handle’s platform: \"email\"."},"ref":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]{1,18}$","description":"A masked handle’s `ref` (get_entry → editing.handles, where its value is null): it names the stored handle without its address."}},"required":["platform_id","ref"]}]}},"image_media_id":{"description":"A new lead image already on the site (media_catalog, get_entry), or one you uploaded held for this proposal (upload_image or upload_image_from_url with hold: true): only its uploader may propose a held image, and the approval releases it.","type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]{1,18}$"},"image_commons_token":{"description":"A new lead image from Wikimedia Commons: a hit’s `token` from search_commons_images. The file is recorded on the site first, as the editor’s picker does.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2000},"clear_image":{"description":"true: take the lead image off. At most one of image_media_id, image_commons_token and clear_image.","type":"boolean"},"gallery":{"description":"The images after the lead: the whole ordered list of media ids, replacing the gallery; [] empties it. At most 5, each once, never the lead.","maxItems":50,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]{1,18}$"}},"relinquish_fields":{"description":"Fields to hand to the Wikidata sync.","maxItems":5,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["title","subtitle","description","image","entity_type"]}},"takeover_fields":{"description":"Fields to take back from the Wikidata sync, keeping their values.","maxItems":5,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["title","subtitle","description","image","entity_type"]}},"relinquish_handles":{"description":"Handles to hand to the Wikidata sync; only while Wikidata lists the value.","maxItems":50,"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"platform_id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The platform id, e.g. \"twitter\": one the platform catalog has (get_entry with include_platforms lists the enabled ones; platform_catalog, every one). A new handle on an unknown or disabled platform is refused (400 invalid_platform)."},"value":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The handle as stored, e.g. \"nasa\"."}},"required":["platform_id","value"]}},"takeover_handles":{"description":"Handles to take back from the Wikidata sync.","maxItems":50,"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"platform_id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The platform id, e.g. \"twitter\": one the platform catalog has (get_entry with include_platforms lists the enabled ones; platform_catalog, every one). A new handle on an unknown or disabled platform is refused (400 invalid_platform)."},"value":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The handle as stored, e.g. \"nasa\"."}},"required":["platform_id","value"]}},"release_held_handles":{"description":"Held-back handles the sync may add back.","maxItems":50,"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"platform_id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The platform id, e.g. \"twitter\": one the platform catalog has (get_entry with include_platforms lists the enabled ones; platform_catalog, every one). A new handle on an unknown or disabled platform is refused (400 invalid_platform)."},"value":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The handle as stored, e.g. \"nasa\"."}},"required":["platform_id","value"]}},"qid":{"description":"The Wikidata item to link the entry to, e.g. \"Q42\" (a different one re-points it); null unlinks it.","anyOf":[{"type":"string","pattern":"^[Qq][1-9][0-9]*$"},{"type":"null"}]},"adopt":{"description":"With qid: the fields the item may manage; the rest are taken back by the site.","maxItems":5,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["title","subtitle","description","image","entity_type"]}},"base_revision_id":{"description":"The revision you read (get_entry → editing.baseRevisionId). If the entry has changed since, the edit is refused as a conflict. Left out, the current revision is used.","type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]+$"},"note":{"description":"Why you propose this, in plain words: posted as the proposal’s first comment, which the reviewer reads with it. At most 2,000 characters. Never an internal tracking ID (a backlog or ticket number); a VHID is fine.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2000},"idempotency_key":{"description":"Optional: a key you choose (1–255 printable ASCII, e.g. a UUID), sent as the write’s Idempotency-Key. Calling again with the same key and the same change within 24 hours answers the first call’s result (replayed: true) and writes nothing; the same key with another change is refused (422).","type":"string","pattern":"^[\\x20-\\x7E]{1,255}$"},"dry_run":{"default":true,"description":"true (the default): write nothing — show the change and the exact request it would send. false: make the change.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["entry"]},"output":{"type":"object","properties":{"dry_run":{"description":"true: a dry run, which wrote nothing. Absent from a real run.","type":"boolean"},"would_send":{"description":"A dry run: the exact request the real run would send (`method`, `path`, any `headers` such as an Idempotency-Key, and its `body`, `form` or `query`), or the requests, in order."},"note":{"description":"A dry run: what to do next to make the change, in words."},"confirm":{"description":"A dry run of a change that needs it: the exact target to send back as `confirm` with dry_run: false.","type":"string"},"replayed":{"description":"A real run with an idempotency_key already used for this change: the first call’s answer, given back; nothing was written now.","type":"boolean","const":true},"may_edit_live":{"description":"A dry run of a live edit: whether this key’s account may edit this entry live.","type":"boolean"},"refused_because":{"description":"A dry run the real run would be refused for: why, in words.","type":"string"},"result":{"description":"A real run: the route’s own answer, where the tool adds facts of its own beside it."}},"additionalProperties":{},"description":"A dry run (`dry_run: true`): what the change would be and the exact request it would send. A real run: what the route answered."}},{"name":"propose_new_entry","title":"Propose a new entry","description":"Propose a new entry for a reviewer to decide: it waits in Console → Applications under Quick proposals (list_applications with tab \"proposals\") and becomes live when approved. Refused (not_accepting) while Settings pauses new-entry requests, unless this account may create entries itself. For someone or something with no Wikidata item, leave out qid. With qid, the entry is linked to that item, and after approval Wikidata keeps up to date whatever you did not write (and any field in let_wikidata_manage). Refused, naming the entry, when one is already on the item. A merged-away QID is refused (409 qid_merged), naming the item Wikidata kept in wikidata_item: propose on that one. Sending the same proposal again within 15 minutes answers with the first one. `note` tells the reviewer why. Audited. Dry run by default: it names the entries already on the item, a short name already taken or held by a site redirect (short_is_redirect), and handles already on another entry.","write":true,"confirm":false,"capabilities":["propose"],"role":null,"keyless":false,"liveEdit":false,"linkImages":false,"input":{"type":"object","properties":{"title":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":500},"subtitle":{"type":"string","maxLength":500},"description":{"description":"HTML; it is sanitised when stored.","type":"string","maxLength":65536},"short":{"description":"The short name, as in verifiedhandles.org/<short>. Whether it is free is checked when the proposal is approved.","type":"string","maxLength":100},"handles":{"maxItems":50,"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"platform_id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The platform id, e.g. \"twitter\": one the platform catalog has (get_entry with include_platforms lists the enabled ones; platform_catalog, every one). A new handle on an unknown or disabled platform is refused (400 invalid_platform)."},"value":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The handle as stored, e.g. \"nasa\"."},"display":{"type":"string","maxLength":200}},"required":["platform_id","value"]}},"qid":{"description":"The Wikidata item, e.g. \"Q42\". Leave it out for an entry with no item.","type":"string","pattern":"^[Qq][1-9][0-9]*$"},"let_wikidata_manage":{"description":"With qid: fields you give that Wikidata should keep up to date after approval, as the console form does for a title it prefilled and you left as it was.","maxItems":3,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["title","subtitle","description"]}},"note":{"description":"Why you propose this, in plain words: posted as the proposal’s first comment, which the reviewer reads with it. At most 2,000 characters. Never an internal tracking ID (a backlog or ticket number); a VHID is fine.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2000},"idempotency_key":{"description":"Optional: a key you choose (1–255 printable ASCII, e.g. a UUID), sent as the write’s Idempotency-Key. Calling again with the same key and the same change within 24 hours answers the first call’s result (replayed: true) and writes nothing; the same key with another change is refused (422).","type":"string","pattern":"^[\\x20-\\x7E]{1,255}$"},"dry_run":{"default":true,"description":"true (the default): write nothing — show the change and the exact request it would send. false: make the change.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["title"]},"output":{"type":"object","properties":{"dry_run":{"description":"true: a dry run, which wrote nothing. Absent from a real run.","type":"boolean"},"would_send":{"description":"A dry run: the exact request the real run would send (`method`, `path`, any `headers` such as an Idempotency-Key, and its `body`, `form` or `query`), or the requests, in order."},"note":{"description":"A dry run: what to do next to make the change, in words."},"confirm":{"description":"A dry run of a change that needs it: the exact target to send back as `confirm` with dry_run: false.","type":"string"},"replayed":{"description":"A real run with an idempotency_key already used for this change: the first call’s answer, given back; nothing was written now.","type":"boolean","const":true},"may_edit_live":{"description":"A dry run of a live edit: whether this key’s account may edit this entry live.","type":"boolean"},"refused_because":{"description":"A dry run the real run would be refused for: why, in words.","type":"string"},"result":{"description":"A real run: the route’s own answer, where the tool adds facts of its own beside it."}},"additionalProperties":{},"description":"A dry run (`dry_run: true`): what the change would be and the exact request it would send. A real run: what the route answered."}},{"name":"report_entry","title":"Report an entry","description":"Report an entry to the Verified Handles team, as its page’s “Report” form does: for a person to decide: delete, merge, image rights, wrong information. Reason `image` names the image it is about (media_id, one of the images the entry shows) and needs a note saying who owns it and what should change. Reason `image_link` is about where an image links (only for an image with a link — get_entry’s images[].link); media_id names which, else the first with one, and the report keeps the link as it is now. To delete or merge an entry, report it as `incorrect` or `other` with a note naming the entry to keep. It lands in Console → Reports. Audited. Dry run by default.","write":true,"confirm":false,"capabilities":[],"role":null,"keyless":false,"liveEdit":false,"linkImages":false,"input":{"type":"object","properties":{"entry":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"pattern":"^(?!\\.{1,2}$)","description":"The entry: its VHID (11 digits), its short name (as in verifiedhandles.org/<short>), or its Wikidata QID (Q42)."},"reason":{"type":"string","enum":["impersonation","incorrect","outdated","abuse","image","image_link","other"],"description":"impersonation: a handle here isn’t the real account; incorrect information; outdated: a handle has changed or closed; abuse or inappropriate content; image: its rights or permission; image_link: where an image links goes somewhere wrong, misleading or harmful; other."},"note":{"description":"What is wrong, for the team (at most 1000 characters). Needed for an image report.","type":"string","maxLength":1000},"media_id":{"description":"For reason `image` or `image_link`: which of the entry’s images (the dry run lists them).","type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]{1,18}$"},"dry_run":{"default":true,"description":"true (the default): write nothing — show the change and the exact request it would send. false: make the change.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["entry","reason"]},"output":{"type":"object","properties":{"dry_run":{"description":"true: a dry run, which wrote nothing. Absent from a real run.","type":"boolean"},"would_send":{"description":"A dry run: the exact request the real run would send (`method`, `path`, any `headers` such as an Idempotency-Key, and its `body`, `form` or `query`), or the requests, in order."},"note":{"description":"A dry run: what to do next to make the change, in words."},"confirm":{"description":"A dry run of a change that needs it: the exact target to send back as `confirm` with dry_run: false.","type":"string"},"replayed":{"description":"A real run with an idempotency_key already used for this change: the first call’s answer, given back; nothing was written now.","type":"boolean","const":true},"may_edit_live":{"description":"A dry run of a live edit: whether this key’s account may edit this entry live.","type":"boolean"},"refused_because":{"description":"A dry run the real run would be refused for: why, in words.","type":"string"},"result":{"description":"A real run: the route’s own answer, where the tool adds facts of its own beside it."}},"additionalProperties":{},"description":"A dry run (`dry_run: true`): what the change would be and the exact request it would send. A real run: what the route answered."}},{"name":"list_my_submissions","title":"My own submissions","description":"This key’s own account’s submissions — proposed changes, new-entry proposals, claims, reports and applications — newest first, 25 a page: each with its status, its entry, when it was sent and decided, and the reviewer’s notes. `status: open` keeps the ones still waiting. With `id`, one submission (yours, or any a reviewer may see) with what it asks and its comment thread.","write":false,"confirm":false,"capabilities":[],"role":null,"keyless":false,"liveEdit":false,"linkImages":false,"input":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"default":"all","type":"string","enum":["open","all"]},"page":{"default":1,"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":10000},"id":{"description":"One submission’s id, from this list or from the tool that sent it.","type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]{1,18}$"}}},"output":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["open","all"]},{"type":"string","enum":["pending","needs_info","approved","rejected","merged","spam","superseded","retracted","resolved"]}]},"page":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":9007199254740991},"per_page":{"type":"number","const":25},"total":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991},"has_next":{"type":"boolean"},"submissions":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\d+$"},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["new_entity","correction","claim","report","application"],"description":"What was asked: a new entry, a change, a claim, a report or an application."},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["pending","needs_info","approved","rejected","merged","spam","superseded","retracted","resolved"]},"entry":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"vhid":{"type":"string"},"short":{"type":["string","null"]},"title":{"type":"string"}},"required":["vhid","short","title"],"additionalProperties":{}},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The entry it is about; null for a new entry or an application."},"qid":{"description":"The Wikidata item it names, if any.","type":["string","null"]},"created_at":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","pattern":"^(?:(?:\\d\\d[2468][048]|\\d\\d[13579][26]|\\d\\d0[48]|[02468][048]00|[13579][26]00)-02-29|\\d{4}-(